1
00:00:18,219 --> 00:00:20,429
(Yeosu)

2
00:00:22,059 --> 00:00:27,099
(By day, a feast of delicious food awaits you.)

3
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:35,769
(By night, romance settles over the city.)

4
00:00:36,639 --> 00:00:40,079
(We return to Yeosu, the city of romance.)

5
00:00:41,979 --> 00:00:43,319
Hello, I'm...

6
00:00:46,749 --> 00:00:49,448
Apparently, a lot of people like me.

7
00:00:49,449 --> 00:00:50,958
Honestly, I don't know why.

8
00:00:50,959 --> 00:00:53,028
(Why he came to visit the siblings)

9
00:00:53,029 --> 00:00:55,359
I don't think she can live without me.

10
00:00:56,499 --> 00:00:59,028
(To stir things up at the siblings')

11
00:00:59,029 --> 00:01:01,599
(a catfish man has arrived.)

12
00:01:02,269 --> 00:01:03,598
(What's your most attractive feature?)

13
00:01:03,599 --> 00:01:05,569
I'm not sure. My charm is...

14
00:01:06,469 --> 00:01:07,669
my big nose.

15
00:01:08,339 --> 00:01:10,009
My nose looks like it'd bring luck.

16
00:01:11,379 --> 00:01:12,838
(Shy)

17
00:01:12,839 --> 00:01:14,479
I hear that quite often.

18
00:01:15,679 --> 00:01:17,549
People just whisper about me...

19
00:01:18,619 --> 00:01:20,949
every time I walk by. Why not just say it to my face?

20
00:01:21,419 --> 00:01:23,218
My goodness.

21
00:01:23,219 --> 00:01:24,659
(The owner of an irresistible charm)

22
00:01:24,719 --> 00:01:25,889
Gosh, it's hot.

23
00:01:26,789 --> 00:01:29,429
(Who's the dangerously charming man who can't handle the heat?)

24
00:01:29,559 --> 00:01:30,919
You look like a catfish on camera.

25
00:01:31,499 --> 00:01:32,729
A catfish is...

26
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:34,569
Isn't that a fish?

27
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:40,609
(The catfish man, Jeong Sang Hun)

28
00:01:40,869 --> 00:01:43,679
(The Lamb Skewers and Tsingtao character on "SNL Korea")

29
00:01:44,039 --> 00:01:45,938
("Mrs. Doubtfire" and "A Gentleman's Guide to Love and Murder")

30
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:48,979
(A veteran musical theater actor who's captivated audiences)

31
00:01:49,949 --> 00:01:51,589
Which celebrity makes me feel threatened?

32
00:01:52,119 --> 00:01:53,189
Cho Jung Seok.

33
00:01:55,119 --> 00:01:56,248
(What kind of friend are you to Jung Ah?)

34
00:01:56,249 --> 00:01:57,359
I'm a cutie.

35
00:01:58,389 --> 00:02:01,189
Jung Ah bothers me a lot because of my charm.

36
00:02:02,229 --> 00:02:06,259
(That's enough.)

37
00:02:06,569 --> 00:02:08,828
I want to make unforgettable memories...

38
00:02:08,829 --> 00:02:10,669
for Fresh off the Sea members.

39
00:02:10,969 --> 00:02:13,909
I want to leave a mark on their lives.

40
00:02:14,669 --> 00:02:15,908
(The catfish man, Jeong San Hun came...)

41
00:02:15,909 --> 00:02:17,709
(to I'm a Single's Inferno at the siblings'.)

42
00:02:17,779 --> 00:02:20,178
- Let me know when you're ready.
- Yes, I'm seated.

43
00:02:20,179 --> 00:02:21,179
Okay.

44
00:02:21,449 --> 00:02:23,848
They'll be so shocked. No one will recognise me.

45
00:02:23,849 --> 00:02:24,849
(What unforgettable memory...)

46
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:26,490
(has Sang Hun prepared for the siblings?)

47
00:02:26,649 --> 00:02:29,049
(A resort in Yeosu)

48
00:02:29,519 --> 00:02:30,689
Gosh, my eyes.

49
00:02:32,189 --> 00:02:33,259
It's so bright.

50
00:02:33,859 --> 00:02:35,829
(Woman No. 1 makes her entrance.)

51
00:02:36,529 --> 00:02:39,359
(Woman No. 1 ascends the stairs gracefully.)

52
00:02:40,399 --> 00:02:41,528
Hello.

53
00:02:41,529 --> 00:02:43,139
(Woman No. 1, Roh Yoon Seo)

54
00:02:43,739 --> 00:02:45,998
(Entering with an impressively enthusiastic greeting)

55
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:47,568
How do I go in?

56
00:02:47,569 --> 00:02:49,268
(Entrance)

57
00:02:49,269 --> 00:02:50,339
Where is...

58
00:02:50,579 --> 00:02:51,638
This way?

59
00:02:51,639 --> 00:02:54,079
(A charmingly awkward woman who gets lost at the entrance)

60
00:02:54,209 --> 00:02:55,579
Oh, it's this way.

61
00:02:55,879 --> 00:02:56,949
Hello.

62
00:02:58,049 --> 00:03:00,419
Hello. It feels very unfamiliar to be in a place like this.

63
00:03:01,519 --> 00:03:03,118
(Looking around)

64
00:03:03,119 --> 00:03:04,319
(Scratching)

65
00:03:04,659 --> 00:03:05,758
It feels very unfamiliar.

66
00:03:05,759 --> 00:03:07,458
(A suspiciously luxurious location for the opening)

67
00:03:07,459 --> 00:03:09,689
(There's even an outdoor swimming pool.)

68
00:03:12,029 --> 00:03:13,829
I feel like we should be filming "EXchange."

69
00:03:16,799 --> 00:03:19,599
The place is so unfamiliar and way too fancy.

70
00:03:20,139 --> 00:03:21,899
I bet there's ulterior motive behind this...

71
00:03:22,469 --> 00:03:23,739
until the end...

72
00:03:25,209 --> 00:03:27,048
It's beautiful, but I'm worried.

73
00:03:27,049 --> 00:03:28,825
(As Yoon Seo grows uneasy in the luxurious place, )

74
00:03:28,849 --> 00:03:31,179
(a woman appears reflected in the window.)

75
00:03:31,949 --> 00:03:33,289
(Smiling)

76
00:03:33,989 --> 00:03:36,219
(She might have been Miss Korea back in the day.)

77
00:03:36,659 --> 00:03:37,689
Jung Ah!

78
00:03:42,259 --> 00:03:43,558
You can't see anything from there.

79
00:03:43,559 --> 00:03:45,199
- I can't see anything.
- Seriously.

80
00:03:45,329 --> 00:03:46,598
- I couldn't see anything.
- Right?

81
00:03:46,599 --> 00:03:47,629
Hi.

82
00:03:48,199 --> 00:03:49,939
Hello. It's been a month.

83
00:03:50,839 --> 00:03:52,069
This place is nice.

84
00:03:52,569 --> 00:03:53,668
It feels unfamiliar.

85
00:03:53,669 --> 00:03:55,538
- We should be filming "EXchange."
- Right.

86
00:03:55,539 --> 00:03:57,609
You're supposed to ask,

87
00:03:58,179 --> 00:04:00,099
"How did you get here?" Isn't that what you ask?

88
00:04:00,209 --> 00:04:01,578
- How did I get here?
- How did you get here?

89
00:04:01,579 --> 00:04:02,978
Is that what you ask, Jung Ah?

90
00:04:02,979 --> 00:04:04,679
Isn't that what they ask on "EXchange?"

91
00:04:05,349 --> 00:04:06,419
Am I wrong?

92
00:04:07,489 --> 00:04:09,019
The show I watched must be...

93
00:04:09,589 --> 00:04:10,919
"Better Late..."

94
00:04:12,089 --> 00:04:13,289
"Than Single."

95
00:04:14,029 --> 00:04:16,389
"Better Late Than Single?" Okay.

96
00:04:17,229 --> 00:04:19,059
On "EXchange," it's more like...

97
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:21,399
"I saw that you went on a date with him yesterday."

98
00:04:22,369 --> 00:04:24,368
"Did you have fun?"

99
00:04:24,369 --> 00:04:25,638
What do they say when they meet for the first time?

100
00:04:25,639 --> 00:04:26,708
When they meet for the first time?

101
00:04:26,709 --> 00:04:27,839
"Hello."

102
00:04:28,139 --> 00:04:30,059
Meanwhile, you scan the person from head to toe.

103
00:04:31,139 --> 00:04:32,178
"Hello."

104
00:04:32,179 --> 00:04:34,108
(Subtle flirting is essential.)

105
00:04:34,109 --> 00:04:36,378
"EXchange" is the one where your exes show up.

106
00:04:36,379 --> 00:04:38,079
That's right.

107
00:04:38,849 --> 00:04:41,089
Gosh, the sunlight...

108
00:04:42,219 --> 00:04:44,588
I should get in the shade.

109
00:04:44,589 --> 00:04:45,618
Hello.

110
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:47,028
(Making her entrance as radiant as the August sunshine)

111
00:04:47,029 --> 00:04:48,669
I didn't see you because of the sunlight.

112
00:04:49,229 --> 00:04:51,959
(Woman No. 3, Kim Sun Young)

113
00:04:53,599 --> 00:04:54,669
Hello.

114
00:04:54,829 --> 00:04:56,169
Hello.

115
00:04:56,799 --> 00:04:58,898
Gosh, this place is so luxurious.

116
00:04:58,899 --> 00:04:59,908
Look at her hands.

117
00:04:59,909 --> 00:05:02,639
- Where should I sit?
- Everyone says the same thing.

118
00:05:03,179 --> 00:05:04,738
My goodness.

119
00:05:04,739 --> 00:05:06,948
- It's so fancy here.
- Doesn't it feel unfamiliar?

120
00:05:06,949 --> 00:05:08,378
Can I get some brunch?

121
00:05:08,379 --> 00:05:09,819
(It doesn't feel unfamiliar at all.)

122
00:05:10,149 --> 00:05:12,778
One iced latte and a croissant, please.

123
00:05:12,779 --> 00:05:15,119
(She just came to have breakfast.)

124
00:05:15,449 --> 00:05:16,718
Why isn't You Seok here?

125
00:05:16,719 --> 00:05:18,419
Has he not arrived yet?

126
00:05:18,959 --> 00:05:20,559
At six in the morning...

127
00:05:20,689 --> 00:05:22,458
- He got here at 6:30am.
- Right.

128
00:05:22,459 --> 00:05:25,159
- He must be very tired.
- He probably didn't get any sleep.

129
00:05:25,729 --> 00:05:28,169
(Fidgeting around)

130
00:05:28,399 --> 00:05:29,969
I've dropped...

131
00:05:30,799 --> 00:05:32,898
a cake before.

132
00:05:32,899 --> 00:05:35,338
(Despite his busy schedule, You Seok came all the way to Yeosu.)

133
00:05:35,339 --> 00:05:36,578
(He prepared a surprise for Jung Ah.)

134
00:05:36,579 --> 00:05:38,539
(He's more excited than she is.)

135
00:05:39,139 --> 00:05:40,679
(Quietly)

136
00:05:41,309 --> 00:05:42,309
What?

137
00:05:42,310 --> 00:05:43,319
(She spots You Seok.)

138
00:05:43,419 --> 00:05:44,479
Is he here?

139
00:05:44,919 --> 00:05:47,048
- Gosh, he brought something.
- What is it?

140
00:05:47,049 --> 00:05:49,169
(Hurrying through the back door so she won't see him)

141
00:05:49,989 --> 00:05:51,058
Where did he go?

142
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,319
I came around the other way.

143
00:05:52,619 --> 00:05:54,129
Right, it's Jung Ah's birthday.

144
00:05:55,489 --> 00:05:57,359
- One, two, three.
- Two, three.

145
00:05:57,859 --> 00:06:00,799
(Happy Birthday to you)

146
00:06:00,999 --> 00:06:03,698
- What happened to your arm?
- Happy Birthday to you

147
00:06:03,699 --> 00:06:04,838
- What's wrong with your arm?
- All right.

148
00:06:04,839 --> 00:06:06,039
Let's celebrate first.

149
00:06:06,139 --> 00:06:09,469
- Happy Birthday to our dear Jung Ah - But...

150
00:06:10,039 --> 00:06:11,838
Happy Birthday to you

151
00:06:11,839 --> 00:06:13,209
- Let me light it.
- My goodness.

152
00:06:13,609 --> 00:06:15,209
Wait, I'll light it.

153
00:06:15,749 --> 00:06:17,719
- While I was...
- Did you make it?

154
00:06:17,819 --> 00:06:19,748
- I didn't make it myself.
- It looks so cute.

155
00:06:19,749 --> 00:06:20,948
- He's so thoughtful.
- Right.

156
00:06:20,949 --> 00:06:23,188
- It looks so cute.
- I'm more worried...

157
00:06:23,189 --> 00:06:24,819
about your arm than this.

158
00:06:24,919 --> 00:06:26,789
During a shoot yesterday,

159
00:06:27,759 --> 00:06:30,859
I slightly fractured my wrist.

160
00:06:31,129 --> 00:06:33,498
It isn't a ligament injury. The doctor said that I could work.

161
00:06:33,499 --> 00:06:34,568
(Worried)

162
00:06:34,569 --> 00:06:36,799
Oh, no. I ruined the mood.

163
00:06:37,199 --> 00:06:39,099
I'm really okay. Don't worry about me.

164
00:06:39,439 --> 00:06:41,108
I'll do my best with one hand.

165
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:42,139
Right, but...

166
00:06:42,909 --> 00:06:44,955
(Holding an emergency meeting about You Seok's injury)

167
00:06:44,979 --> 00:06:47,349
He bumped his arm a little.

168
00:06:48,049 --> 00:06:50,549
He said that it wasn't anything to worry about.

169
00:06:51,219 --> 00:06:53,178
- And...
- He's injured.

170
00:06:53,179 --> 00:06:54,619
We can't make him work.

171
00:06:55,519 --> 00:06:59,459
(They decide to keep an eye on him through the opening shoot.)

172
00:06:59,489 --> 00:07:02,358
This is our final shoot in Yeosu.

173
00:07:02,359 --> 00:07:03,359
Okay.

174
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:05,299
It's sad. I had a dream about it.

175
00:07:05,499 --> 00:07:07,468
A few days ago, I dreamed about our fourth shoot.

176
00:07:07,469 --> 00:07:10,198
I even saw our guest.

177
00:07:10,199 --> 00:07:11,839
- Who was it?
- Who was the guest?

178
00:07:12,799 --> 00:07:13,838
Jae Wook came.

179
00:07:13,839 --> 00:07:14,868
- Then I thought, - Lee Jae Wook?

180
00:07:14,869 --> 00:07:15,869
- He's in the military.
- "He's in the military."

181
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:17,285
- When I got up in the morning, - He's in the military.

182
00:07:17,309 --> 00:07:19,109
I was about to send a message to the members.

183
00:07:19,139 --> 00:07:21,349
I thought, "But he's in the military."

184
00:07:21,479 --> 00:07:24,219
You must have Dex and Jae Wook on your mind a lot.

185
00:07:25,019 --> 00:07:26,019
Don't say that.

186
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,048
- Especially yesterday...
- Dex and...

187
00:07:27,049 --> 00:07:29,719
- He was on a show.
- On a show yesterday...

188
00:07:29,889 --> 00:07:32,359
I like you, Dex.

189
00:07:32,419 --> 00:07:34,589
- Right, you like Dex.
- I really like him.

190
00:07:34,859 --> 00:07:36,058
He isn't coming today, is it?

191
00:07:36,059 --> 00:07:38,258
- I really miss him.
- Are you wary of him?

192
00:07:38,259 --> 00:07:39,359
No, not at all.

193
00:07:39,829 --> 00:07:41,399
If he comes, I won't say a word.

194
00:07:42,229 --> 00:07:43,369
What is he saying?

195
00:07:47,169 --> 00:07:50,708
Speaking of guests...

196
00:07:50,709 --> 00:07:53,079
- Do we have a guest today?
- He's already here.

197
00:07:53,349 --> 00:07:55,108
- Right here?
- Why are you telling us that?

198
00:07:55,109 --> 00:07:57,078
- Right here?
- Here?

199
00:07:57,079 --> 00:07:59,448
- Why is she telling us that?
- Where are you?

200
00:07:59,449 --> 00:08:00,719
Do we have to find him?

201
00:08:01,489 --> 00:08:03,419
- Why is she telling us that?
- Is he hiding?

202
00:08:03,619 --> 00:08:05,619
- Right here?
- Is he wearing a hat? Hold on.

203
00:08:06,059 --> 00:08:07,158
- The camera...
- What?

204
00:08:07,159 --> 00:08:08,289
Isn't he wearing a hat?

205
00:08:08,659 --> 00:08:11,128
Hold on. We have to look at each of them...

206
00:08:11,129 --> 00:08:12,629
- He's wearing a hat.
- carefully.

207
00:08:13,569 --> 00:08:14,569
Where could he be?

208
00:08:15,069 --> 00:08:17,199
- There's someone suspicious.
- What's that?

209
00:08:17,439 --> 00:08:18,868
- You startled me.
- Where?

210
00:08:18,869 --> 00:08:19,899
- There he is.
- What?

211
00:08:20,909 --> 00:08:22,139
- Gosh, what's that?
- Where?

212
00:08:23,879 --> 00:08:25,179
- Gosh, what's that?
- Where?

213
00:08:25,339 --> 00:08:26,339
- You startled me.
- What?

214
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:27,408
- You startled me.
- What?

215
00:08:27,409 --> 00:08:28,709
- Where?
- There he is.

216
00:08:29,449 --> 00:08:30,779
(What's going on here?)

217
00:08:31,049 --> 00:08:32,969
- It's a woman.
- It must be. She has long hair.

218
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:34,588
Her ankles look very thin.

219
00:08:34,589 --> 00:08:35,889
(Long hair and thin ankles)

220
00:08:36,719 --> 00:08:38,758
(Answer: Jeong Sang Hun with a wig)

221
00:08:38,759 --> 00:08:41,028
- Our guest has arrived.
- Her ankles...

222
00:08:41,029 --> 00:08:42,789
- Right.
- Have a seat first.

223
00:08:43,399 --> 00:08:45,629
Please sit down. Don't go near the guest.

224
00:08:45,929 --> 00:08:47,068
(Staring)

225
00:08:47,069 --> 00:08:48,729
Hey, Cha Joo Young. Come out.

226
00:08:49,069 --> 00:08:50,715
- Is it Cha Joo Young?
- Isn't it Cha Joo Young?

227
00:08:50,739 --> 00:08:52,999
(Jeong Sang Hun)

228
00:08:53,269 --> 00:08:54,909
When did you prepare all this?

229
00:08:55,239 --> 00:08:56,985
- My field of vision is very narrow.
- We invited...

230
00:08:57,009 --> 00:08:59,308
- a special mystery guest.
- Do we guess who it is?

231
00:08:59,309 --> 00:09:01,708
If you can figure out who it is by asking ten questions,

232
00:09:01,709 --> 00:09:04,649
- we'll give you a dining voucher.
- Okay.

233
00:09:05,179 --> 00:09:06,349
- What?
- Really?

234
00:09:07,249 --> 00:09:08,318
Seriously?

235
00:09:08,319 --> 00:09:10,788
But you can only ask ten questions.

236
00:09:10,789 --> 00:09:12,519
- Okay. Ten should be enough.
- Okay.

237
00:09:12,689 --> 00:09:14,729
Doesn't the hair look like a wig?

238
00:09:15,029 --> 00:09:16,928
How old are you?

239
00:09:16,929 --> 00:09:18,559
Hello.

240
00:09:19,029 --> 00:09:21,269
- It's nice to meet you.
- What did he say?

241
00:09:21,529 --> 00:09:22,529
- He says he's happy to meet us.
- "It's nice to meet you."

242
00:09:22,530 --> 00:09:23,598
(A mysteriously distorted voice)

243
00:09:23,599 --> 00:09:25,169
(Laughing)

244
00:09:25,539 --> 00:09:29,469
I've been waiting for over an hour.

245
00:09:29,669 --> 00:09:31,638
- What?
- He waited for over an hour.

246
00:09:31,639 --> 00:09:33,178
- Really?
- Yes.

247
00:09:33,179 --> 00:09:35,849
- He must be hot. I feel bad.
- You Seok.

248
00:09:36,149 --> 00:09:37,949
- You Seok?
- Nice to meet you.

249
00:09:38,149 --> 00:09:40,049
It must be someone who knows you.

250
00:09:40,389 --> 00:09:41,449
Do you know me?

251
00:09:42,019 --> 00:09:45,019
Of course. I'm your huge fan.

252
00:09:45,219 --> 00:09:47,888
After watching "When Life Gives You Tangerines,"

253
00:09:47,889 --> 00:09:51,499
I fell in love with you.

254
00:09:53,529 --> 00:09:55,269
He refuses to answer the question.

255
00:09:55,499 --> 00:09:56,668
(He talks about whatever he wants.)

256
00:09:56,669 --> 00:09:58,299
How old are you?

257
00:09:58,999 --> 00:10:00,239
- It sounds like...
- I am...

258
00:10:00,769 --> 00:10:04,078
around the same age as Yoon Seo.

259
