(The road leads them to farmland.)

514
00:19:30,239 --> 00:19:31,919
- I wonder what we're doing.
- What is it?

515
00:19:32,139 --> 00:19:34,878
Oh, my. We arrived, and it's absolutely scorching.

516
00:19:34,879 --> 00:19:35,948
- But still...
- What's this?

517
00:19:35,949 --> 00:19:37,525
(Blazing sunlight without even a single cloud)

518
00:19:37,549 --> 00:19:38,949
What's here anyway?

519
00:19:39,979 --> 00:19:40,989
Everyone, get out.

520
00:19:41,449 --> 00:19:42,889
- Let's get out immediately.
- Gosh.

521
00:19:43,589 --> 00:19:46,489
The moment I stepped out, I could feel paradise and inferno.

522
00:19:47,159 --> 00:19:48,159
(The heat hits them the second they step outside.)

523
00:19:48,159 --> 00:19:49,159
This is incredible.

524
00:19:49,359 --> 00:19:52,028
- What could possibly be here?
- Today's sun...

525
00:19:52,029 --> 00:19:53,098
It's no joke.

526
00:19:53,099 --> 00:19:54,668
I didn't even bring a hat.

527
00:19:54,669 --> 00:19:56,109
(Literally sweltering under the sun)

528
00:19:56,569 --> 00:19:58,998
- There's no cloud in sight.
- Not even a single cloud.

529
00:19:58,999 --> 00:20:00,375
(The sun beats down from the cloudless sky.)

530
00:20:00,399 --> 00:20:01,439
Gosh, it's hot.

531
00:20:01,569 --> 00:20:03,068
- The green onions are dying.
- It's hot.

532
00:20:03,069 --> 00:20:04,555
(The sunlight is so intense they can barely open their eyes.)

533
00:20:04,579 --> 00:20:05,579
Come into the shade.

534
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:06,908
I hope we get to work in the shade. Right?

535
00:20:06,909 --> 00:20:07,909
This is unbelievable.

536
00:20:07,910 --> 00:20:09,155
(They walk along the shade to avoid the sun.)

537
00:20:09,179 --> 00:20:10,378
- What?
- What is it?

538
00:20:10,379 --> 00:20:12,119
(It seems like they're almost there.)

539
00:20:12,279 --> 00:20:14,248
Are we picking corn? Waxy corn?

540
00:20:14,249 --> 00:20:15,969
(What work will they do on such a hot day?)

541
00:20:16,149 --> 00:20:18,618
(Looking around)

542
00:20:18,619 --> 00:20:19,619
Chili pepper?

543
00:20:21,089 --> 00:20:22,328
It's a chilli pepper field.

544
00:20:22,329 --> 00:20:24,699
(Rows of chilli peppers greet them along the way to labour.)

545
00:20:25,029 --> 00:20:27,468
The chilli peppers are ripe and red.

546
00:20:27,469 --> 00:20:28,469
They're so beautiful.

547
00:20:28,969 --> 00:20:30,568
- The spicy smell hits you.
- Is it red pepper?

548
00:20:30,569 --> 00:20:31,669
- Yes.
- Red pepper.

549
00:20:32,139 --> 00:20:34,908
Today's harvest will be...

550
00:20:34,909 --> 00:20:36,969
Yeosu's fiery red specialty, chilli peppers.

551
00:20:37,369 --> 00:20:38,379
Really?

552
00:20:39,439 --> 00:20:42,509
(Today's labour, harvesting chilli peppers)

553
00:20:42,879 --> 00:20:44,619
(Speaking of Anpo Village's chilli peppers)

554
00:20:46,349 --> 00:20:48,118
They're surrounded by mountains...

555
00:20:48,119 --> 00:20:49,918
with the sea on one side.

556
00:20:49,919 --> 00:20:51,719
(Thanks to the sea breeze from the South Sea)

557
00:20:52,419 --> 00:20:54,388
They grow quite well.

558
00:20:54,389 --> 00:20:56,365
(Known for their vivid red colour and clean, fiery taste)

559
00:20:56,389 --> 00:21:00,399
The chilli peppers are sown between April 15 and 25.

560
00:21:00,969 --> 00:21:03,429
(Once the flowers fall, green chilli peppers begin to grow.)

561
00:21:03,869 --> 00:21:06,098
(Leave bright green peppers hanging for more than a month, )

562
00:21:06,099 --> 00:21:08,209
(and they transform into red chilli peppers.)

563
00:21:08,669 --> 00:21:11,209
(All you need to do is pick them by hand with a quick snap.)

564
00:21:11,479 --> 00:21:14,879
(So it looks like a simple job, )

565
00:21:15,409 --> 00:21:18,349
(but there's a hidden catch.)

566
00:21:18,749 --> 00:21:20,889
(As the full-blown summer heat sets in, )

567
00:21:21,549 --> 00:21:25,759
(a heat wave warning was issued all over Yeosu.)

568
00:21:26,459 --> 00:21:31,129
(Chili pepper harvesting in the middle of a heat wave)

569
00:21:31,529 --> 00:21:32,758
It's hot.

570
00:21:32,759 --> 00:21:34,279
(The camera director exhales heavily.)

571
00:21:34,699 --> 00:21:35,728
I can't keep filming anymore.

572
00:21:35,729 --> 00:21:37,045
(Even the staff is shocked by the heat.)

573
00:21:37,069 --> 00:21:39,745
(With the low-hanging branches forcing them to work crouched down, )

574
00:21:39,769 --> 00:21:42,269
(it's far more gruelling than any other farm work.)

575
00:21:42,669 --> 00:21:44,979
(It's the ultimate farm work.)

576
00:21:45,409 --> 00:21:47,309
(The size of today's chilli pepper field)

577
00:21:47,879 --> 00:21:50,979
(It's about 661m².)

578
00:21:51,679 --> 00:21:54,549
(Will the siblings make it through the chilli pepper harvest safely?)

579
00:21:54,849 --> 00:21:56,488
- Gosh, hello.
- Hello.

580
00:21:56,489 --> 00:21:57,718
- Hello.
- Hello.

581
00:21:57,719 --> 00:21:58,719
- Hello.
- Hello.

582
00:21:58,720 --> 00:21:59,765
(Helping them with today's farm work is Kim Hyo Ja.)

583
00:21:59,789 --> 00:22:01,729
- When picking chilli peppers, - Right.

584
00:22:01,959 --> 00:22:03,759
You don't pick the green ones.

585
00:22:04,299 --> 00:22:05,659
You only pick the red ones.

586
00:22:06,429 --> 00:22:08,069
These are the ones we eat fresh.

587
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:11,468
If you pick these and dry them...

588
00:22:11,469 --> 00:22:12,938
- They become dried chilli peppers?
- Yes.

589
00:22:12,939 --> 00:22:14,615
- They're made into chilli powder.
- Chili powder.

590
00:22:14,639 --> 00:22:17,739
- You can't pick those, right?
- They have a mix of colours.

591
00:22:19,109 --> 00:22:20,109
Green ones?

592
00:22:20,110 --> 00:22:21,155
(Chili peppers with a mix of colours)

593
00:22:21,179 --> 00:22:23,749
- Not the ones with mixed colours.
- You can't pick those.

594
00:22:24,819 --> 00:22:27,059
Don't pick the green ones. Only pick the fully red ones.

595
00:22:27,479 --> 00:22:29,449
(Grip the stem with both hands)

596
00:22:29,919 --> 00:22:30,919
(Give it a firm tug and snap it)

597
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:32,689
You take the whole stem off?

598
00:22:33,889 --> 00:22:36,258
The ripe ones are a little softer.

599
00:22:36,259 --> 00:22:38,019
They're nice and smooth when you grind them.

600
00:22:38,529 --> 00:22:41,049
(Once you get the hang of it, you can pick them with one hand.)

601
00:22:41,469 --> 00:22:43,599
(After harvesting the chilli peppers, )

602
00:22:43,999 --> 00:22:46,669
(put them into the mesh bags according to weight)

603
00:22:47,069 --> 00:22:49,609
(Go ahead and pick them neatly)

604
00:22:49,969 --> 00:22:51,078
The completely red ones...

605
00:22:51,079 --> 00:22:52,278
Only the fully red ones.

606
00:22:52,279 --> 00:22:53,338
I see.

607
00:22:53,339 --> 00:22:55,808
- I got it. Thank you.
- Go ahead and pick them.

608
00:22:55,809 --> 00:22:56,849
Thank you.

609
00:22:56,979 --> 00:22:58,149
How much is it per mesh bag?

610
00:22:58,879 --> 00:23:01,589
- Each mesh bag holds 5kg.
- Okay.

611
00:23:01,889 --> 00:23:04,818
We'll pay you 20 dollars per mesh bag.

612
00:23:04,819 --> 00:23:05,819
Twenty dollars per mesh bag?

613
00:23:05,820 --> 00:23:06,888
(Their pay is 20 dollars per bag.)

614
00:23:06,889 --> 00:23:09,528
In order to earn 100 dollars,

615
00:23:09,529 --> 00:23:12,129
- we have to fill 5 bags.
- we need to fill 2 boxes, right?

616
00:23:12,899 --> 00:23:13,998
Take a bucket.

617
00:23:13,999 --> 00:23:15,899
- Everyone grabs a bucket.
- Yes.

618
00:23:16,729 --> 00:23:19,968
Gosh, let's give it a try.

619
00:23:19,969 --> 00:23:20,969
(Let's just try it.)

620
00:23:22,239 --> 00:23:25,178
(Following what they've been taught, )

621
00:23:25,179 --> 00:23:28,909
(they grip the stem and pull to snap the chilli pepper.)

622
00:23:29,309 --> 00:23:32,319
(She masters the art of picking chilli in one go.)

623
00:23:32,749 --> 00:23:34,919
(You Seok also gives it a try.)

624
00:23:36,349 --> 00:23:41,089
(The chilli peppers come right off.)

625
00:23:41,389 --> 00:23:42,689
(Like this)

626
00:23:42,829 --> 00:23:47,999
(Carefully harvesting the peppers without damaging them)

627
00:23:48,569 --> 00:23:50,629
Is the sunlight what makes them turn red?

628
00:23:52,599 --> 00:23:56,239
(To help the peppers ripen into a deep red)

629
00:23:56,909 --> 00:23:57,978
(There's no shade on the chilli pepper field.)

630
00:23:57,979 --> 00:23:59,109
The sun is really intense.

631
00:24:00,039 --> 00:24:01,378
I'm already drenched in sweat.

632
00:24:01,379 --> 00:24:03,699
(Just 5 minutes into the job, their sweat glands explode.)

633
00:24:03,779 --> 00:24:07,119
(Gosh, it's hot.)

634
00:24:07,419 --> 00:24:10,489
You should all take a nice shower when you get home.

635
00:24:10,989 --> 00:24:11,989
Of course.

636
00:24:12,419 --> 00:24:14,328
Some of them don't wash themselves.

637
00:24:14,329 --> 00:24:15,769
Jung Ah, what are you talking about?

638
00:24:16,089 --> 00:24:17,775
We didn't take a shower only once last time.

639
00:24:17,799 --> 00:24:19,499
There was a perfectly good reason.

640
00:24:19,899 --> 00:24:21,228
We were going into a creek.

641
00:24:21,229 --> 00:24:22,328
The water was clean.

642
00:24:22,329 --> 00:24:23,469
I want to go to a creek.

643
00:24:24,439 --> 00:24:26,268
On a day like today, I want to jump right in.

644
00:24:26,269 --> 00:24:27,269
I want to go there too.

645
00:24:27,270 --> 00:24:28,539
I want to dive right in.

646
00:24:29,569 --> 00:24:32,478
(Putting their thoughts on a refreshing creek aside)

647
00:24:32,479 --> 00:24:33,479
Goodness.

648
00:24:34,579 --> 00:24:37,979
(They focus on the chilli pepper harvest right in front of them.)

649
00:24:38,849 --> 00:24:41,319
(Gosh, it's beautiful.)

650
00:24:41,449 --> 00:24:44,118
Picking chilli peppers is actually really fun.

651
00:24:44,119 --> 00:24:45,718
- I like it.
- Yes.

652
00:24:45,719 --> 00:24:46,919
I like it because it's simple.

653
00:24:47,659 --> 00:24:50,388
There's something satisfying about the spicy smell.

654
00:24:50,389 --> 00:24:51,399
- Right.
- Yes.

655
00:24:51,859 --> 00:24:53,198
They're very fresh.

656
00:24:53,199 --> 00:24:57,669
(Everyone is completely absorbed in picking chilli peppers.)

657
00:24:57,839 --> 00:24:59,768
The chilli peppers are very plump.

658
00:24:59,769 --> 00:25:01,138
- They're very big.
- Right?

659
00:25:01,139 --> 00:25:03,538
Yes, they're very red too.

660
00:25:03,539 --> 00:25:05,709
(Big, bright red chilli peppers that are ripe)

661
00:25:05,839 --> 00:25:08,108
It's so shiny.

662
00:25:08,109 --> 00:25:09,379
(Glossy)

663
00:25:09,949 --> 00:25:12,549
Look, it's this big.

664
00:25:12,619 --> 00:25:13,778
(Some are as big as Yoon Seo's face.)

665
00:25:13,779 --> 00:25:14,889
It's as big as my palm.

666
00:25:15,449 --> 00:25:17,348
The more I pick them, the more they look like fruit.

667
00:25:17,349 --> 00:25:19,019
They look beautiful and appetizing.

668
00:25:19,989 --> 00:25:22,128
I had no idea that chilli peppers could be this pretty.

669
00:25:22,129 --> 00:25:24,088
- Right, Sun Young?
- They're so pretty.

670
00:25:24,089 --> 00:25:25,228
And they're huge.

671
00:25:25,229 --> 00:25:26,675
(Captivated by the charms of gorgeous chilli peppers)

672
00:25:26,699 --> 00:25:28,369
They have to be bright red.

673
00:25:29,099 --> 00:25:30,868
You have to pick only the fully red ones.

674
00:25:30,869 --> 00:25:32,299
(Picking the reddest chilli peppers)

675
00:25:32,839 --> 00:25:35,268
(The siblings give it their all.)

676
00:25:35,269 --> 00:25:36,909
There are so many.

677
00:25:37,439 --> 00:25:40,778
(Even when it gets tough, they keep their spirits high.)

678
00:25:40,779 --> 00:25:44,208
It's nice doing this while chatting quietly.

679
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:45,219
Isn't it nice?

680
00:25:46,079 --> 00:25:48,588
Sang Hun, what is it called?

681
00:25:48,589 --> 00:25:49,788
Who's Sang Hun?

682
00:25:49,789 --> 00:25:51,659
- Isn't he Sang Hun?
- Who?

683
00:25:51,989 --> 00:25:54,388
- I'm Ssang Soon.
- Ssang Soon.

684
00:25:54,389 --> 00:25:56,529
And I like chilli peppers.

685
00:25:58,729 --> 00:25:59,849
What are you saying exactly?

686
00:26:00,329 --> 00:26:03,099
- What are you saying?
- Here we go again.

687
00:26:03,299 --> 00:26:06,998
- Gosh, that's embarrassing.
- There he goes again.

688
00:26:06,999 --> 00:26:08,338
It's small but spicy.

689
00:26:08,339 --> 00:26:10,209
Goodness, I don't know.

690
00:26:10,739 --> 00:26:13,139
(The atmosphere starts heating up.)

691
00:26:13,279 --> 00:26:16,109
This chilli pepper field is definitely spicy.

692
00:26:16,309 --> 00:26:17,829
- It's spicy.
- It's definitely spicy.

693
00:26:18,379 --> 00:26:20,418
Chili peppers arrived in Korea...

694
00:26:20,419 --> 00:26:21,949
much later than the Joseon dynasty.

695
00:26:22,249 --> 00:26:24,288
- Really?
- It was a foreign crop.

696
00:26:24,289 --> 00:26:25,388
Is that so?

697
00:26:25,389 --> 00:26:27,749
(The Useless but Interesting Encyclopedia of Chili Peppers)

698
00:26:27,959 --> 00:26:30,328
So we didn't originally have chilli powder?

699
00:26:30,329 --> 00:26:31,958
Exactly. We used to only make white kimchi.

700
00:26:31,959 --> 00:26:33,198
Apparently, we only had white kimchi in the past.

701
00:26:33,199 --> 00:26:34,928
Is that true? My goodness.

702
00:26:34,929 --> 00:26:36,898
(A theory that chilli peppers were introduced to Korea through Japan)

703
00:26:36,899 --> 00:26:38,598
- I had no idea.
- That's right.

704
00:26:38,599 --> 00:26:39,599
My goodness.

705
00:26:39,899 --> 00:26:41,569
Who brought this red vegetable to Korea?

706
00:26:43,439 --> 00:26:44,509
Was it Mun Ik Chom?

707
00:26:45,109 --> 00:26:47,439
(I'm not sure about that part.)

708
00:26:47,849 --> 00:26:50,379
(Laughing)

709
00:26:50,849 --> 00:26:53,618
(Mun Ik Chom brought cotton seeds.)

710
00:26:53,619 --> 00:26:55,819
(That's hilarious.)

711
00:26:56,549 --> 00:26:57,988
- Gosh.
- "Was it Mun Ik Chom?"

712
00:26:57,989 --> 00:26:59,018
(He must've been busy bringing cotton seeds and chilli peppers.)

713
00:26:59,019 --> 00:27:00,059
Goodness.

714
00:27:00,389 --> 00:27:01,688
He said that it was Mun Ik Chom.

715
00:27:01,689 --> 00:27:03,105
(His knowledge is wide yet shallow.)

716
00:27:03,129 --> 00:27:05,128
(20 minutes into their labour work)

717
00:27:05,129 --> 00:27:06,398
(Groaning)

718
00:27:06,399 --> 00:27:07,728
(Exclaiming)

719
00:27:07,729 --> 00:27:09,428
Gosh, it's burning hot.

720
00:27:09,429 --> 00:27:10,468
(With time, the heat gets increasingly intense.)

721
00:27:10,469 --> 00:27:11,569
It's really hot.

722
00:27:12,539 --> 00:27:14,459
I can really feel the heat now that I'm working.

723
00:27:15,509 --> 00:27:17,978
The ones buried deep inside are so hard to pick.

724
00:27:17,979 --> 00:27:19,539
- You can't reach them, right?
- Right.

725
00:27:20,309 --> 00:27:22,508
They're so tangled up.

726
00:27:22,509 --> 00:27:25,025
(Red chilli peppers are hiding deep inside the tangled branches.)

727
00:27:25,049 --> 00:27:26,648
They're all hiding.

728
00:27:26,649 --> 00:27:28,919
If they were hanging outside, I'd pick them much faster.

729
00:27:29,489 --> 00:27:31,488
It'd be easier if you could see them easily.

730
00:27:31,489 --> 00:27:33,158
- They're hiding.
- I have to reach my hand...

731
00:27:33,159 --> 00:27:34,928
- far inside. This is hard.
- It's hard.

732
00:27:34,929 --> 00:27:35,929
I can't speed up.

733
00:27:36,629 --> 00:27:37,629
Are they here?

734
00:27:37,630 --> 00:27:41,469
(Red chilli peppers, where are you hiding?)

735
00:27:41,829 --> 00:27:43,629
(On the other hand, )

736
00:27:43,869 --> 00:27:48,439
(You Seok is good at picking only the red chilli peppers.)

737
00:27:49,239 --> 00:27:53,739
(Every single one he picks is a bright red chilli pepper.)

738
00:27:53,979 --> 00:27:55,499
I have a chilli pepper field back home.

739
00:27:56,309 --> 00:27:58,849
(It turns out that he's the chilli pepper prince.)

740
00:27:58,919 --> 00:28:00,559
But you've never done this before, right?

741
00:28:01,019 --> 00:28:02,089
Of course not.

742
00:28:03,619 --> 00:28:05,365
I thought that it was easy, so I never helped out.

743
00:28:05,389 --> 00:28:07,905
- Because you thought it was easy?
- That's why you didn't help out?

744
00:28:07,929 --> 00:28:09,159
Because it's easy.

745
00:28:09,689 --> 00:28:11,059
Mother and Father.

746
00:28:11,959 --> 00:28:13,299
Your bad son is crying.

747
00:28:13,999 --> 00:28:16,469
He should've helped out knowing that it was hard work.

748
00:28:17,969 --> 00:28:19,668
(The chilli pepper prince picks chilli peppers...)

749
00:28:19,669 --> 00:28:21,569
(as if seeking redemption.)

750
00:28:21,969 --> 00:28:24,269
(Working hard)

751
00:28:24,739 --> 00:28:27,509
(You Seok's basket is filling up with red chilli peppers.)

752
00:28:27,979 --> 00:28:31,449
(He's still harvesting nonstop.)

753
00:28:31,679 --> 00:28:34,079
You Seok, look at her. Look how fast she is.

754
00:28:37,749 --> 00:28:40,389
(Threatening the chilli pepper prince)

755
00:28:41,159 --> 00:28:44,629
Gosh, we're good at this work.

756
00:28:45,459 --> 00:28:46,798
(Picking 2 while others pick only 1)

757
00:28:46,799 --> 00:28:48,499
(The difference in speed is clear.)

758
00:28:48,729 --> 00:28:50,329
I'll work even faster.

759
00:28:51,799 --> 00:28:54,080
(The chilli peppers are piling up at an incredible speed.)

760
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:56,739
Watching this show yesterday, I realised...

761
00:28:57,309 --> 00:28:58,579
how great Yoon Seo is at work.

762
00:28:59,009 --> 00:29:00,455
When she was harvesting sea squirt...

763
00:29:00,479 --> 00:29:01,479
- and...
- This is no big deal.

764
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:03,509
- She's smart.
- Also when she dug garlic.

765
00:29:04,349 --> 00:29:07,549
(Once she clears them out hiding inside the branches)

766
00:29:07,679 --> 00:29:09,389
I'm done.

767
00:29:09,589 --> 00:29:10,818
She's really good.

768
00:29:10,819 --> 00:29:12,265
(She's the first one to fill the entire bucket.)

769
00:29:12,289 --> 00:29:14,518
I'll dump them inside the basket for now.

770
00:29:14,519 --> 00:29:16,639
(They'll put them in mesh bags later and weigh them.)

771
00:29:17,789 --> 00:29:19,958
Yes, we'll take care of them later.

772
00:29:19,959 --> 00:29:21,575
(Yoon Seo did a good job picking only the red, ripe peppers.)

773
00:29:21,599 --> 00:29:24,939
I'm confident when it comes to using my hands.

774
00:29:25,769 --> 00:29:27,099
She studied art.

775
00:29:27,439 --> 00:29:29,339
- Is that so?
- She studied art.

776
00:29:29,939 --> 00:29:31,009
I also...

777
00:29:31,409 --> 00:29:34,179
used to draw back in the day.

778
00:29:34,579 --> 00:29:36,879
- Ssang Soon, did you draw too?
- That's right.

779
00:29:37,009 --> 00:29:38,218
I'm good at drawing.

780
00:29:38,219 --> 00:29:39,919
So you have amazing hand skills.

781
00:29:40,479 --> 00:29:44,019
(Picking out only the bright red chilli peppers)

782
00:29:45,159 --> 00:29:47,359
Gosh, I filled up one bucket already.

783
00:29:48,089 --> 00:29:51,459
(Being an art major gives you some impressive hand skills.)

784
00:29:51,829 --> 00:29:54,699
(I'd better hurry up too.)

785
00:29:55,099 --> 00:29:57,969
(When you snap and pick each chilli pepper)

786
00:29:58,339 --> 00:30:00,438
(Before you know it, everyone has filled their bucket.)

787
00:30:00,439 --> 00:30:01,668
Everyone is working so fast.

788
00:30:01,669 --> 00:30:05,639
(Before you know it, everyone has filled their bucket.)

789
00:30:06,679 --> 00:30:08,078
The colour is really beautiful.

790
00:30:08,079 --> 00:30:10,159
(Within 30 minutes, they fill up one yellow basket.)

791
00:30:10,379 --> 00:30:11,848
Now that I'm standing up,

792
00:30:11,849 --> 00:30:15,088
the field we have to harvest is no joke.

793
00:30:15,089 --> 00:30:16,089
(It's huge.)

794
00:30:16,349 --> 00:30:18,719
- It won't be easy.
- Right. We have to pick them fast.

795
00:30:19,959 --> 00:30:23,389
(They work with both hands as fast as possible.)

796
00:30:27,059 --> 00:30:28,229
Gosh, it's hot.

797
00:30:28,999 --> 00:30:29,999
(Exhaling)

798
00:30:30,369 --> 00:30:31,369
(Panting)

799
00:30:31,399 --> 00:30:32,838
(The heat is closing in on them more and more.)

800
00:30:32,839 --> 00:30:33,969
Gosh, it's hard.

801
00:30:34,839 --> 00:30:36,879
(The current temperature at the chilli pepper field)

802
00:30:37,309 --> 00:30:38,439
The weather is insane.

803
00:30:39,539 --> 00:30:41,479
When you stand up, there's a bit of breeze.

804
00:30:42,579 --> 00:30:45,019
Goodness, I wish they wouldn't be hiding.

805
00:30:46,279 --> 00:30:49,149
There's no wind. The heat is radiating from the ground.

806
00:30:50,019 --> 00:30:51,918
- Doesn't it feel like 40°C today?
- It's hotter.

807
00:30:51,919 --> 00:30:53,365
(It's 1 of the hottest days ever on Fresh off the Sea 3.)

808
00:30:53,389 --> 00:30:57,459
(Their faces are turning bright red.)

809
00:30:57,789 --> 00:30:59,259
Gosh, this is exhausting.

810
00:30:59,829 --> 00:31:01,429
My sweat is pouring down.

811
00:31:02,729 --> 00:31:03,729
(Beads of sweat)

812
00:31:03,730 --> 00:31:04,898
I'm drenched in sweat.

813
00:31:04,899 --> 00:31:06,599
(Wiping away the running sweat)

814
00:31:07,969 --> 00:31:09,009
Goodness.

815
00:31:10,239 --> 00:31:13,039
(His sweat keeps dripping, and he can't do anything about it.)

816
00:31:13,409 --> 00:31:15,209
(Under the blazing sun)

817
00:31:15,579 --> 00:31:16,748
I'm sweating on my back.

818
00:31:16,749 --> 00:31:18,818
(The siblings are getting exhausted at an alarming rate.)

819
00:31:18,819 --> 00:31:20,249
I'm dizzy. I feel like throwing up.

820
00:31:23,719 --> 00:31:26,418
(The sight of me crying)

821
00:31:26,419 --> 00:31:29,128
(I look so pathetic)

822
00:31:29,129 --> 00:31:30,828
(I hate this)

823
00:31:30,829 --> 00:31:33,128
(Bright, blazing sun)

824
00:31:33,129 --> 00:31:34,928
(Gasping)

825
00:31:34,929 --> 00:31:36,628
(Exclaiming)

826
00:31:36,629 --> 00:31:39,799
(It's insanely hot.)

827
00:31:40,099 --> 00:31:41,139
I'm sweating...

828
00:31:41,769 --> 00:31:42,909
like crazy.

829
00:31:43,839 --> 00:31:48,349
(Is it sweat or tears?)

830
00:31:48,849 --> 00:31:50,148
I'm about to collapse.

831
00:31:50,149 --> 00:31:51,849
(Very close to collapsing)

832
00:31:52,349 --> 00:31:56,019
Can I get a sip of cold water?

833
00:31:56,749 --> 00:32:01,788
(After rehydrating with life-saving water, )

834
00:32:01,789 --> 00:32:06,459
(After rehydrating with life-saving water, )

835
00:32:06,899 --> 00:32:10,468
(they get back to work.)

836
00:32:10,469 --> 00:32:11,569
It's so hot.

837
00:32:13,369 --> 00:32:15,969
The spiciness from the chilli peppers is hitting my face.

838
00:32:16,569 --> 00:32:19,309
It really feels spicy now.

839
00:32:20,809 --> 00:32:22,478
(Sneezing)

840
00:32:22,479 --> 00:32:23,908
- Isn't it because it's spicy?
- Gosh, yes.

841
00:32:23,909 --> 00:32:25,355
(It's so spicy that it makes him sneeze.)

842
00:32:25,379 --> 00:32:26,979
It's hot and spicy. It's total chaos.

843
00:32:28,849 --> 00:32:30,689
What's our goal for today?

844
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:33,489
- Forty kilograms.
- Forty kilograms?

845
00:32:33,989 --> 00:32:36,458
- Per mesh bag...
- We earn 20 dollars per bag.

846
00:32:36,459 --> 00:32:37,459
(Are you serious?)

847
00:32:37,789 --> 00:32:40,459
I don't think chilli peppers weigh that much.

848
00:32:41,259 --> 00:32:44,368
I think 2 buckets will fill 1 bag.

849
00:32:44,369 --> 00:32:45,809
(Will they be able to harvest 40kg?)

850
00:32:45,899 --> 00:32:47,069
I'm not tired.

851
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:48,938
Not even a little.

852
00:32:48,939 --> 00:32:50,619
(50 minutes into the chilli pepper harvest)

853
00:32:51,109 --> 00:32:53,938
My brain isn't sending commands to my fingers anymore.

854
00:32:53,939 --> 00:32:55,649
(Because it's too hot)

855
00:32:56,479 --> 00:32:57,479
(Exhaling)

856
00:32:58,149 --> 00:32:59,149
(Turning)

857
00:32:59,150 --> 00:33:01,079
Honey, when are we quitting?

858
00:33:01,319 --> 00:33:04,919
Honey, I want to quit first.

859
00:33:06,559 --> 00:33:07,559
She's possessed.

860
00:33:07,560 --> 00:33:08,588
- Sun Young, what are you saying?
- Honey.

861
00:33:08,589 --> 00:33:10,988
- She's possessed by a baby ghost.
- I'll go back to Seoul first.

862
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:12,589
- She's possessed by a ghost.
- Goodbye.

863
00:33:12,759 --> 00:33:14,098
- Take care.
- Sun Young.

864
00:33:14,099 --> 00:33:16,339
- Sun Young, are you okay?
- She's possessed by a ghost.

865
00:33:16,469 --> 00:33:18,469
Hey, it's a bee. Go away.

866
00:33:19,469 --> 00:33:20,569
Go away.

867
00:33:21,469 --> 00:33:23,308
- Go away.
- Get away.

868
00:33:23,309 --> 00:33:24,668
- Leave.
- Get away.

869
00:33:24,669 --> 00:33:26,079
(Everyone has lost their mind.)

870
00:33:26,379 --> 00:33:28,578
Eat this before you go.

871
00:33:28,579 --> 00:33:29,948
(Feeling sorry)

872
00:33:29,949 --> 00:33:31,079
Eat this.

873
00:33:31,279 --> 00:33:32,579
Eat it before you go, you punk.

874
00:33:33,749 --> 00:33:34,749
"Eat it before you go?"

875
00:33:34,750 --> 00:33:36,289
(You're scaring me.)

876
00:33:36,619 --> 00:33:38,789
(70 minutes into the labour work)

877
00:33:39,119 --> 00:33:40,719
How is everyone doing? Is it manageable?

878
00:33:41,159 --> 00:33:42,289
It's not manageable.

879
00:33:43,089 --> 00:33:44,458
- It's not, right?
- It's very hard.

880
00:33:44,459 --> 00:33:45,459
Right.

881
00:33:46,329 --> 00:33:49,469
It feels like someone has to collapse before we can finish.

882
00:33:50,499 --> 00:33:51,969
Let's play rock-paper-scissors.

883
00:33:52,899 --> 00:33:53,968
- Do you want to do it, Sang Hun?
- What?

884
00:33:53,969 --> 00:33:55,569
Why don't you do it?

885
00:33:56,039 --> 00:33:57,409
Here's what I'll do.

886
00:33:58,069 --> 00:34:00,879
Japan collapsing. The US collapsing.

887
00:34:01,779 --> 00:34:03,109
India collapsing.

888
00:34:04,009 --> 00:34:05,119
Shall I start with the US?

889
00:34:06,049 --> 00:34:07,278
Don't look at him.

890
00:34:07,279 --> 00:34:08,888
Keep working and react when he does it.

891
00:34:08,889 --> 00:34:10,519
Here he goes. Ready, action.

892
00:34:13,719 --> 00:34:14,759
Hey, sun.

893
00:34:15,089 --> 00:34:16,229
Oh, my gosh.

894
00:34:16,729 --> 00:34:17,859
Oh, my gosh!

895
00:34:19,029 --> 00:34:21,229
(Hollywood-level acting)

896
00:34:21,599 --> 00:34:22,628
Oh, my gosh!

897
00:34:22,629 --> 00:34:24,868
(American reactions exploding left and right)

898
00:34:24,869 --> 00:34:26,269
- Oh, my gosh.
- That's okay.

899
00:34:26,939 --> 00:34:28,068
Oh, my gosh.

900
00:34:28,069 --> 00:34:29,238
(Fainting attempt number 2)

901
00:34:29,239 --> 00:34:31,109
That's okay. I'm okay.

902
00:34:31,569 --> 00:34:33,879
(The American man looks quite fragile.)

903
00:34:34,179 --> 00:34:36,409
- That was the US.
- The US.

904
00:34:37,049 --> 00:34:38,049
This is Japan.

905
00:34:38,050 --> 00:34:39,219
(Next is Japan.)

906
00:34:39,779 --> 00:34:40,779
(Breathing)

907
00:34:41,219 --> 00:34:42,289
I feel...

908
00:34:43,119 --> 00:34:44,719
(The rainy road hurts.)

909
00:34:45,119 --> 00:34:50,059
(Everyone bursts out laughing.)

910
00:34:50,489 --> 00:34:52,929
- What about India?
- India.

911
00:34:53,399 --> 00:34:55,129
(Anticipating)

912
00:34:55,599 --> 00:34:56,898
(What is everyone doing without working?)

913
00:34:56,899 --> 00:34:58,219
(Hurry and pick chilli peppers...)

914
00:34:58,539 --> 00:34:59,539
(Hakaiyomo)

915
00:34:59,869 --> 00:35:01,908
(Let's just dance.)

916
00:35:01,909 --> 00:35:02,909
(Laughing)

917
00:35:02,910 --> 00:35:04,839
(Let's just dance.)

918
00:35:05,109 --> 00:35:07,439
(Shake it)

919
00:35:07,839 --> 00:35:10,478
(This is exciting.)

920
00:35:10,479 --> 00:35:12,248
Did you do India, Japan, and the US?

921
00:35:12,249 --> 00:35:13,318
I did them all.

922
00:35:13,319 --> 00:35:14,548
- Can you do China too?
- China?

923
00:35:14,549 --> 00:35:16,249
- I forgot about China.
- Yes, China.

924
00:35:16,649 --> 00:35:18,758
China is the land of martial arts.

925
00:35:18,759 --> 00:35:19,789
- Right.
- Yes.

926
00:35:21,959 --> 00:35:22,959
(Exclaiming)

927
00:35:23,359 --> 00:35:24,359
(Speaking Chinese)

928
00:35:24,489 --> 00:35:29,229
(This is the spirit of the Chinese continent.)

929
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:31,329
(Laughing)

930
00:35:31,869 --> 00:35:33,699
My knees are stinging.

931
00:35:35,069 --> 00:35:36,769
- Seriously...
- Gosh, Sang Hun.

932
00:35:37,209 --> 00:35:39,079
Even in this heat,

933
00:35:39,739 --> 00:35:41,925
he's putting his whole body into it just to make us laugh.

934
00:35:41,949 --> 00:35:43,078
He's so funny.

935
00:35:43,079 --> 00:35:45,319
(Thanks to Sang Hun who went all out to make them laugh)

936
00:35:45,479 --> 00:35:46,919
Once you get into it,

937
00:35:47,249 --> 00:35:48,588
- It gets done fast?
- it's over before you know it.

938
00:35:48,589 --> 00:35:51,959
(The siblings gather their strength and get back to work.)

939
00:35:52,259 --> 00:35:53,389
- Yoon Seo.
- Yes?

940
00:35:53,489 --> 00:35:55,559
- Let me know when you're done.
- Why?

941
00:35:56,659 --> 00:35:58,089
I'll carry yours over there.

942
00:35:59,859 --> 00:36:00,899
Give it to me.

943
00:36:01,769 --> 00:36:03,098
- It's okay.
- I'll take it.

944
00:36:03,099 --> 00:36:04,099
(She refuses once.)

945
00:36:04,100 --> 00:36:05,168
Seriously?

946
00:36:05,169 --> 00:36:06,598
(She reluctantly accepts the offer.)

947
00:36:06,599 --> 00:36:08,999
What if they start having feelings for each other like this?

948
00:36:09,739 --> 00:36:10,869
- Yoon Seo.
- Yes?

949
00:36:10,939 --> 00:36:12,819
I'll make an acrostic poem with "chilli pepper."

950
00:36:13,079 --> 00:36:14,109
"Chili."

951
00:36:14,509 --> 00:36:16,679
Yoon Seo, the prettiest one in the chilli pepper field.

952
00:36:17,309 --> 00:36:18,449
Oh, come on.

953
00:36:18,749 --> 00:36:20,219
My gosh.

954
00:36:20,649 --> 00:36:21,718
Goodness.

955
00:36:21,719 --> 00:36:23,589
(Is this really possible?)

956
00:36:23,889 --> 00:36:25,158
- "Pepper."
- She's pathetic.

957
00:36:25,159 --> 00:36:26,788
(She's pathetic.)

958
00:36:26,789 --> 00:36:27,819
Hey!

959
00:36:28,289 --> 00:36:29,928
(Upset)

960
00:36:29,929 --> 00:36:31,488
Stick to the concept.

961
00:36:31,489 --> 00:36:32,829
I was switching it up.

962
00:36:33,129 --> 00:36:34,258
Yoon Seo, I'll try again.

963
00:36:34,259 --> 00:36:35,775
(Trying again while keeping the flirting concept)

964
00:36:35,799 --> 00:36:37,569
- "Chili."
- Good job, Yoon Seo.

965
00:36:38,229 --> 00:36:39,398
(Will you do it right this time?)

966
00:36:39,399 --> 00:36:40,898
- "Pepper."
- That's pathetic.

967
00:36:40,899 --> 00:36:41,909
(Laughing)

968
00:36:42,039 --> 00:36:43,109
It's not funny.

969
00:36:43,739 --> 00:36:45,715
- Have you been hit with a pepper?
- Comedy is all about repetition.

970
00:36:45,739 --> 00:36:47,438
(The flirtation might turn into a fight.)

971
00:36:47,439 --> 00:36:49,749
- The concept completely fell apart.
- That won't work.

972
00:36:50,549 --> 00:36:52,518
You're not supposed to flirt on a chilli pepper field.

973
00:36:52,519 --> 00:36:54,319
(Laughing)

974
00:36:54,679 --> 00:36:56,789
(Ssang Soon must be very lonely.)

975
00:36:57,249 --> 00:36:59,435
I'm getting the hang of this. I can do it with one hand.

976
00:36:59,459 --> 00:37:01,059
- Are you getting the hang of it?
- Yes.

977
00:37:01,989 --> 00:37:04,959
(Yoon Seo can do it easily with one hand.)

978
00:37:06,059 --> 00:37:08,229
It snaps when I do it. One more.

979
00:37:08,669 --> 00:37:10,099
I can tell just by touching them.

980
00:37:10,899 --> 00:37:12,469
Whether they're ripe or not.

981
00:37:13,269 --> 00:37:16,169
After picking so many, you start to develop a knack for it.

982
00:37:17,369 --> 00:37:18,578
(Although they're covered in sweat)

983
00:37:18,579 --> 00:37:19,579
(Sighing)

984
00:37:20,579 --> 00:37:21,579
(Moaning)

985
00:37:21,580 --> 00:37:22,678
I'll pick one more...

986
00:37:22,679 --> 00:37:24,279
before I collapse.

987
00:37:25,419 --> 00:37:27,849
It's hard, but we have to do it.

988
00:37:28,919 --> 00:37:31,149
Everyone, don't complain just because it's hot.

989
00:37:31,959 --> 00:37:33,188
Summer is supposed to be hot.

990
00:37:33,189 --> 00:37:34,719
(Harvesting without taking a break)

991
00:37:35,329 --> 00:37:37,128
(Picking...)

992
00:37:37,129 --> 00:37:39,259
(and picking)

993
00:37:39,829 --> 00:37:42,269
(Beads of sweat form under their chins.)

994
00:37:42,429 --> 00:37:44,299
It's spicy and hot. It's absolute chaos.

995
00:37:44,499 --> 00:37:45,539
My gosh.

996
00:37:46,399 --> 00:37:48,639
(They keep picking nonstop.)

997
00:37:50,039 --> 00:37:51,509
Gosh, we went far.

998
00:37:53,379 --> 00:37:55,348
(The heat is impossible to get used to.)

999
00:37:55,349 --> 00:37:56,879
I should wait.

1000
00:37:58,179 --> 00:38:00,779
(Wiping away the sweat)

1001
00:38:01,179 --> 00:38:03,788
(If they grit their teeth and keep pushing until the end)

1002
00:38:03,789 --> 00:38:05,458
(Exhaling)

1003
00:38:05,459 --> 00:38:07,165
(If they grit their teeth and keep pushing until the end)

1004
00:38:07,189 --> 00:38:12,329
(The chilli peppers pile up in the basket.)

1005
00:38:12,829 --> 00:38:16,269
(Pouring after pouring)

1006
00:38:16,769 --> 00:38:21,469
(Once they move the last bucket and pour it in)

1007
00:38:21,799 --> 00:38:22,908
(They filled 3 baskets after 1 hour and 30 minutes of work.)

1008
00:38:22,909 --> 00:38:25,179
It's done. We're done.

1009
00:38:25,979 --> 00:38:28,009
We harvested a lot. Don't you think?

1010
00:38:28,549 --> 00:38:30,348
Sang Hun is completely drenched.

1011
00:38:30,349 --> 00:38:33,578
(He showered in sweat.)

1012
00:38:33,579 --> 00:38:35,618
- Come and have some snacks.
- They're calling us for a snack.

1013
00:38:35,619 --> 00:38:37,125
- It's a snack.
- Aren't you sweating?

1014
00:38:37,149 --> 00:38:38,389
My goodness.

1015
00:38:38,589 --> 00:38:39,859
(Sweating bullets)

1016
00:38:40,359 --> 00:38:42,189
I didn't even realise that the snack arrived.

1017
00:38:43,359 --> 00:38:45,559
There's a snack? That's incredible.

1018
00:38:46,059 --> 00:38:47,099
What is it?

1019
00:38:47,899 --> 00:38:49,569
Gosh, what's this?

1020
00:38:49,829 --> 00:38:51,045
- What is it?
- It looks great.

1021
00:38:51,069 --> 00:38:52,539
Gosh, it's something refreshing.

1022
00:38:53,799 --> 00:38:54,898
It's leaf mustard.

1023
00:38:54,899 --> 00:38:56,745
(A specialty of Yeosu, leaf mustard mul kimchi)

1024
00:38:56,769 --> 00:38:59,138
It's leaf mustard with acorn jelly.

1025
00:38:59,139 --> 00:39:00,699
(An unusual combination of acorn jelly)

1026
00:39:02,979 --> 00:39:05,879
(Leaf mustard mul kimchi with acorn jelly)

1027
00:39:08,549 --> 00:39:11,889
(For dessert, a perfectly juicy watermelon)

1028
00:39:12,259 --> 00:39:13,359
Gosh, what's this?

1029
00:39:14,689 --> 00:39:15,758
(Cold coffee to wash away the fatigue)

1030
00:39:15,759 --> 00:39:16,788
This is amazing.

1031
00:39:16,789 --> 00:39:18,309
(Cold coffee to wash away the fatigue)

1032
00:39:18,429 --> 00:39:21,559
(Sun Young goes straight for the watermelon.)

1033
00:39:21,759 --> 00:39:24,040
- Leaf mustard and acorn jelly.
- The watermelon is good.

1034
00:39:24,429 --> 00:39:27,739
(She's inhaling it.)

1035
00:39:29,139 --> 00:39:30,968
Are you eating dessert already?

1036
00:39:30,969 --> 00:39:32,309
(Bursting out laughing)

1037
00:39:32,409 --> 00:39:34,039
- You eat dessert first.
- Right.

1038
00:39:34,379 --> 00:39:36,449
- Isn't this an appetizer?
- I didn't know that.

1039
00:39:37,079 --> 00:39:39,148
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you.

1040
00:39:39,149 --> 00:39:41,125
(After the appetizer, it's time to start the meal.)

1041
00:39:41,149 --> 00:39:42,149
It looks delicious.

1042
00:39:42,150 --> 00:39:44,670
(Taking a spoonful of leaf mustard mul kimchi with acorn jelly)

1043
00:39:50,529 --> 00:39:51,529
It's delicious.

1044
00:39:52,559 --> 00:39:56,199
(Drinking up the sweet and sour broth from the bowl)

1045
00:39:56,299 --> 00:39:58,199
(So refreshing)

1046
00:39:58,699 --> 00:40:01,168
So this is leaf mustard kimchi with acorn jelly.

1047
00:40:01,169 --> 00:40:03,209
- Leaf mustard with acorn jelly.
- That must be it.

1048
00:40:03,469 --> 00:40:05,979
- I never had these together.
- Me neither.

1049
00:40:06,539 --> 00:40:07,539
It's so good.

1050
00:40:08,579 --> 00:40:10,249
(Jung Ah also takes a refreshing bite.)

1051
00:40:11,579 --> 00:40:13,379
(It cools you all the way down to your core.)

1052
00:40:13,579 --> 00:40:15,018
That slightly bitter taste of the leaf mustard is...

1053
00:40:15,019 --> 00:40:16,139
(There are no words for it.)

1054
00:40:16,389 --> 00:40:18,489
The mustard leaf aroma is incredible.

1055
00:40:19,659 --> 00:40:22,059
(Slurping in the mustard leaf)

1056
00:40:22,689 --> 00:40:25,188
- Is this leaf mustard kimchi?
- Leaf mustard in the summer...

1057
00:40:25,189 --> 00:40:26,198
(A refreshing summer specialty from Yeosu)

1058
00:40:26,199 --> 00:40:28,259
It must be something like leaf mustard mul kimchi.

1059
00:40:31,499 --> 00:40:32,539
It's very good.

1060
00:40:35,069 --> 00:40:38,269
(The perfect combo of crisp leaf mustard and chewy acorn jelly)

1061
00:40:38,909 --> 00:40:39,909
It's delicious.

1062
00:40:41,009 --> 00:40:42,249
Gosh, this is good.

1063
00:40:43,249 --> 00:40:44,749
- It's refreshing.
- This is good.

1064
00:40:47,179 --> 00:40:48,349
Gosh, this is good.

1065
00:40:48,649 --> 00:40:50,049
(You can't imagine how good it is.)

1066
00:40:50,819 --> 00:40:52,119
This is really tasty.

1067
00:40:53,559 --> 00:40:55,729
(Gulping it down)

1068
00:40:56,689 --> 00:40:59,059
(Gulping it down again)

1069
00:41:01,699 --> 00:41:03,369
(Glancing)

1070
00:41:03,729 --> 00:41:06,398
Did you just finish... the broth in one go?

1071
00:41:06,399 --> 00:41:08,098
- I love broth.
- He must love broth.

1072
00:41:08,099 --> 00:41:10,369
He finished the broth. Do you want some more?

1073
00:41:11,339 --> 00:41:12,778
- I'll give you some more.
- If you leave some...

1074
00:41:12,779 --> 00:41:15,079
(Giving a refill to the broth lover)

1075
00:41:16,949 --> 00:41:18,349
- Thank you.
- Sure.

1076
00:41:19,049 --> 00:41:20,379
(They keep the concept going.)

1077
00:41:21,319 --> 00:41:23,149
(Straight to another sip of broth)

1078
00:41:23,749 --> 00:41:25,018
- Is it good?
- Yes.

1079
00:41:25,019 --> 00:41:27,059
- It's so good.
- It's delicious.

1080
00:41:27,989 --> 00:41:30,088
Our kids definitely love Korean food.

1081
00:41:30,089 --> 00:41:31,458
- Yes, that's right.
- Yes.

1082
00:41:31,459 --> 00:41:33,359
- I've always liked acorn jelly.
- Me too.

1083
00:41:33,599 --> 00:41:35,439
- It's very good with leaf mustard.
- I agree.

1084
00:41:35,829 --> 00:41:36,968
There's also chilli pepper.

1085
00:41:36,969 --> 00:41:38,069
(Whoosh)

1086
00:41:38,299 --> 00:41:41,499
- Gosh, the wind is blowing.
- The wind is blowing.

1087
00:41:42,239 --> 00:41:43,309
It feels so cool.

1088
00:41:44,509 --> 00:41:48,009
(A cool breeze comes by for a moment.)

1089
00:41:48,409 --> 00:41:50,379
Just a little breeze feels so good.

1090
00:41:51,679 --> 00:41:54,349
Who knew this could make me so happy?

1091
00:41:57,619 --> 00:41:58,858
(Taking a little time to relax)

1092
00:41:58,859 --> 00:41:59,859
It's delicious.

1093
00:42:01,289 --> 00:42:02,489
(Exhausted)

1094
00:42:03,159 --> 00:42:04,559
What are we doing after work today?

1095
00:42:05,359 --> 00:42:06,429
You'll get your free time.

1096
00:42:06,659 --> 00:42:07,698
You're lying.

1097
00:42:07,699 --> 00:42:08,699
(Suspicious)

1098
00:42:08,799 --> 00:42:10,429
Don't say that. Just trust her.

1099
00:42:11,099 --> 00:42:12,869
- Okay. Really?
- Don't say anything.

1100
00:42:13,439 --> 00:42:15,238
- That's great.
- Don't say anything.

1101
00:42:15,239 --> 00:42:17,469
I'll scold those who come up with ideas today.

1102
00:42:18,009 --> 00:42:19,909
- A creek...
- Be quiet!

1103
00:42:20,179 --> 00:42:21,179
Creek...

1104
00:42:21,180 --> 00:42:22,949
Don't you have many things you want to do?

1105
00:42:23,909 --> 00:42:24,909
Me?

1106
00:42:25,009 --> 00:42:27,149
- Don't say it.
- Be quiet.

1107
00:42:27,249 --> 00:42:28,449
Creek...

1108
00:42:28,579 --> 00:42:31,518
You Seok, you only slept two hours last night.

1109
00:42:31,519 --> 00:42:32,519
Creek...

1110
00:42:32,520 --> 00:42:35,118
You Seok only got two hours of sleep. He needs some rest.

1111
00:42:35,119 --> 00:42:37,358
- Right.
- I'm not saying this for myself.

1112
00:42:37,359 --> 00:42:38,529
I'm doing it for you.

1113
00:42:39,329 --> 00:42:40,359
I'm okay.

1114
00:42:40,999 --> 00:42:42,269
(Really?)

1115
00:42:42,999 --> 00:42:44,699
(I'm fine.)

1116
00:42:45,199 --> 00:42:47,769
Let's give each other a neck-and-back rinse today.

1117
00:42:48,839 --> 00:42:49,839
What's the matter?

1118
00:42:50,139 --> 00:42:51,209
(Gasping)

1119
00:42:51,539 --> 00:42:53,909
Sure, we can just blur it.

1120
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,379
That would be embarrassing.

1121
00:42:57,149 --> 00:42:58,178
"Blur it?"

1122
00:42:58,179 --> 00:43:00,279
- Seriously.
- It's the same at a bathhouse.

1123
00:43:00,379 --> 00:43:01,918
- About being naked...
- Then everyone has to get naked.

1124
00:43:01,919 --> 00:43:03,519
- Why should only we get naked?
- Right.

1125
00:43:04,089 --> 00:43:06,118
- Then let's all strip...
- After work...

1126
00:43:06,119 --> 00:43:07,158
Instant coffee.

1127
00:43:07,159 --> 00:43:09,188
Let's stop by a supermarket.

1128
00:43:09,189 --> 00:43:11,429
We'll go to the supermarket without washing up.

1129
00:43:11,629 --> 00:43:13,175
- Okay.
- What are we having for dinner?

1130
00:43:13,199 --> 00:43:15,999
We'll make chicken stew with ripened kimchi that we got last time.

1131
00:43:16,569 --> 00:43:18,128
I'd absolutely love that.

1132
00:43:18,129 --> 00:43:20,738
Sang Hun, can you make us a dish?

1133
00:43:20,739 --> 00:43:23,469
- I can make several if you want.
- Your hidden weapon.

1134
00:43:24,439 --> 00:43:25,609
(Anticipating)

1135
00:43:26,039 --> 00:43:27,578
We'll go to the supermarket...

1136
00:43:27,579 --> 00:43:29,078
- and buy some ingredients.
- Okay.

1137
00:43:29,079 --> 00:43:30,109
That sounds great.

1138
00:43:30,949 --> 00:43:33,319
Shall we go to the supermarket now? One, two, three. Go.

1139
00:43:33,749 --> 00:43:34,949
(The packing starts.)

1140
00:43:35,049 --> 00:43:36,889
The snack time is disappearing naturally.

1141
00:43:37,449 --> 00:43:38,489
Let's start parking.

1142
00:43:39,589 --> 00:43:40,989
- Jung Ah, stay seated.
- Yoon Seo.

1143
00:43:41,259 --> 00:43:43,359
- Stay seated.
- Stay seated, Jung Ah.

1144
00:43:43,459 --> 00:43:45,898
- I'll do it. Everyone, sit down.
- You can't do everything yourself.

1145
00:43:45,899 --> 00:43:47,339
- I want to do it too.
- I'm greedy.

1146
00:43:47,499 --> 00:43:48,729
Right. Dex...

1147
00:43:50,237 --> 00:43:52,876
- I'll do it. Everyone, sit down.
- You can't do everything yourself.

1148
00:43:52,877 --> 00:43:54,317
- I want to do it too.
- I'm greedy.

1149
00:43:54,377 --> 00:43:55,677
Right. Dex...

1150
00:43:57,477 --> 00:43:58,707
Right. Dex...

1151
00:43:59,817 --> 00:44:00,876
Dex...

1152
00:44:00,877 --> 00:44:02,117
(Who?)

1153
00:44:02,787 --> 00:44:03,847
(Giving her a look)

1154
00:44:03,947 --> 00:44:05,417
(The name slipped out of her mouth.)

1155
00:44:06,687 --> 00:44:08,457
(Never mind...)

1156
00:44:08,717 --> 00:44:10,626
She said the forbidden name.

1157
00:44:10,627 --> 00:44:11,687
(Flustered)

1158
00:44:11,987 --> 00:44:14,096
I guess coming to Yeosu makes you think...

1159
00:44:14,097 --> 00:44:16,197
about Jae Wook and Dex a lot.

1160
00:44:17,097 --> 00:44:19,267
(Kang You Seok)

1161
00:44:19,567 --> 00:44:21,236
- If you open it, I'll put them in.
- Okay.

1162
00:44:21,237 --> 00:44:22,443
(He calms down and starts packing.)

1163
00:44:22,467 --> 00:44:23,536
Fill it up.

1164
00:44:23,537 --> 00:44:25,113
(Putting the chilli peppers into the mesh bag)

1165
00:44:25,137 --> 00:44:26,607
I'll help you from the side.

1166
00:44:28,137 --> 00:44:31,146
- Could you just hold it for me?
- This won't work.

1167
00:44:31,147 --> 00:44:32,593
(Sang Hun and Yoon Seo, Sun Young and You Seok)

1168
00:44:32,617 --> 00:44:34,217
- They're green.
- Do I leave them out?

1169
00:44:35,217 --> 00:44:36,386
Goodness.

1170
00:44:36,387 --> 00:44:38,463
(Scoop them up nice and generously and transfer them over)

1171
00:44:38,487 --> 00:44:39,617
You're good at packing them.

1172
00:44:40,417 --> 00:44:41,586
(A handful)

1173
00:44:41,587 --> 00:44:43,487
You have big hands.

1174
00:44:44,157 --> 00:44:45,257
You have big hands.

1175
00:44:47,257 --> 00:44:51,327
(Yoon Seo's all-purpose hands are shining again today.)

1176
00:44:53,937 --> 00:44:55,066
We might get ten bags.

1177
00:44:55,067 --> 00:44:56,707
- Right? We'll be fine.
- Yes.

1178
00:44:58,707 --> 00:45:00,436
There are more than I thought.

1179
00:45:00,437 --> 00:45:02,597
(Despite the scorching weather, they harvested a lot.)

1180
00:45:03,377 --> 00:45:06,117
(Jung Ah watches the younger ones working.)

1181
00:45:06,377 --> 00:45:07,977
His underwear is showing.

1182
00:45:08,277 --> 00:45:09,987
(Underwear)

1183
00:45:10,447 --> 00:45:12,786
That's probably fashion. People wear them like that on purpose now.

1184
00:45:12,787 --> 00:45:14,556
- Sagging?
- Don't you know about sagging?

1185
00:45:14,557 --> 00:45:15,956
- I don't know.
- I did it on purpose.

1186
00:45:15,957 --> 00:45:17,663
- They show underwear on purpose.
- Really?

1187
00:45:17,687 --> 00:45:19,847
- It's a trendy fashion style.
- Then show more of it.

1188
00:45:20,057 --> 00:45:21,726
(Sagging)

1189
00:45:21,727 --> 00:45:22,997
(Looking away)

1190
00:45:24,127 --> 00:45:25,227
How many bags do you have?

1191
00:45:25,967 --> 00:45:27,997
We got two bags for now. We have a lot left.

1192
00:45:28,497 --> 00:45:29,567
We'll get three bags.

1193
00:45:31,737 --> 00:45:34,676
As long as we pack one more...

1194
00:45:34,677 --> 00:45:36,377
We harvested a lot.

1195
00:45:37,847 --> 00:45:39,477
Did they say 20 dollars per mesh bag?

1196
00:45:40,247 --> 00:45:41,316
Twenty dollars.

1197
00:45:41,317 --> 00:45:43,947
Oh, my. We earned a lot of money.

1198
00:45:44,717 --> 00:45:46,487
We might have more than ten bags.

1199
00:45:47,487 --> 00:45:48,987
(There are still so many.)

1200
00:45:49,357 --> 00:45:50,426
If we have ten mesh bags,

1201
00:45:50,427 --> 00:45:52,107
- we'll make 200 dollars.
- Give it to me.

1202
00:45:52,957 --> 00:45:53,997
If we don't have enough...

1203
00:45:54,957 --> 00:45:56,467
We didn't expect you to pick so many.

1204
00:45:57,197 --> 00:45:59,667
- We worked very hard.
- Why are you always surprised?

1205
00:46:00,637 --> 00:46:03,707
We always harvest more than you expect.

1206
00:46:03,807 --> 00:46:04,867
That's right.

1207
00:46:04,967 --> 00:46:06,206
They're genuinely surprised.

1208
00:46:06,207 --> 00:46:07,883
(The siblings became professional hard workers.)

1209
00:46:07,907 --> 00:46:08,977
This will be 5kg.

1210
00:46:10,477 --> 00:46:12,476
- It might be over 5kg.
- There are so many green ones.

1211
00:46:12,477 --> 00:46:13,516
Isn't it exactly 5kg?

1212
00:46:13,517 --> 00:46:14,517
(Accurate)

1213
00:46:15,247 --> 00:46:16,286
(A human scale that measures exactly 5kg)

1214
00:46:16,287 --> 00:46:17,287
This is 5kg.

1215
00:46:18,287 --> 00:46:19,457
This is quite a lot too.

1216
00:46:20,217 --> 00:46:21,487
(Accurate again)

1217
00:46:22,017 --> 00:46:23,027
(Weighing)

1218
00:46:23,327 --> 00:46:24,327
This must be 4kg.

1219
00:46:25,457 --> 00:46:26,697
Sang Hun is accurate.

1220
00:46:27,757 --> 00:46:30,227
(Once the human scale fills the mesh bag)

1221
00:46:31,027 --> 00:46:32,997
(Yoon Seo struggles to carry it while sniffling.)

1222
00:46:36,567 --> 00:46:37,567
It's 5kg.

1223
00:46:37,568 --> 00:46:39,248
(It's accurate without a single gram off.)

1224
00:46:40,177 --> 00:46:43,447
(When you aren't sure about the mesh bag's weight)

1225
00:46:44,047 --> 00:46:45,847
- Seven...
- Do I have to add more, Sang Hun?

1226
00:46:46,277 --> 00:46:47,417
Yes, you have to add more.

1227
00:46:47,717 --> 00:46:50,016
- Should I add more here too?
- Yes.

1228
00:46:50,017 --> 00:46:51,547
The other one is okay.

1229
00:46:52,517 --> 00:46:56,027
If you fill it up to the end without tapping it, it'll be exactly 5kg.

1230
00:46:56,857 --> 00:46:57,887
- Okay.
- Yes.

1231
00:46:59,527 --> 00:47:03,397
(Their work speed keeps picking up.)

1232
00:47:05,427 --> 00:47:06,636
I told you we were good.

1233
00:47:06,637 --> 00:47:07,866
I'm the grandson of a farmer.

1234
00:47:07,867 --> 00:47:09,427
(The last box is already nearly empty.)

1235
00:47:11,967 --> 00:47:13,376
- We reached our target.
- Ten?

1236
00:47:13,377 --> 00:47:14,437
Yes.

1237
00:47:14,977 --> 00:47:16,046
We got ten bags.

1238
00:47:16,047 --> 00:47:17,947
(A big harvest at a glance)

1239
00:47:18,547 --> 00:47:20,577
(The last bag of peppers goes on the scale.)

1240
00:47:21,047 --> 00:47:22,047
(Packing is done.)

1241
00:47:22,048 --> 00:47:23,886
- Good.
- How many bags are there?

1242
00:47:23,887 --> 00:47:25,346
- Eleven.
- One, two, three, four...

1243
00:47:25,347 --> 00:47:26,456
- Eleven bags.
- Eleven bags.

1244
00:47:26,457 --> 00:47:27,716
Eight, nine, ten, eleven.

1245
00:47:27,717 --> 00:47:29,527
- It's 55kg.
- They did 11 bags.

1246
00:47:29,957 --> 00:47:31,787
- Since it's 55kg...
- We did 55kg.

1247
00:47:32,327 --> 00:47:33,897
- It's 55kg.
- How much is that?

1248
00:47:34,897 --> 00:47:35,927
Goodness.

1249
00:47:36,627 --> 00:47:39,537
Great work on harvesting the peppers.

1250
00:47:39,637 --> 00:47:40,967
(Feeling proud)

1251
00:47:40,997 --> 00:47:43,367
You're not crying, are you? Don't cry.

1252
00:47:44,067 --> 00:47:45,147
You're not crying, are you?

1253
00:47:45,537 --> 00:47:49,177
(Handing over the pepper shipping fee)

1254
00:47:49,377 --> 00:47:51,746
One, two, three, four,

1255
00:47:51,747 --> 00:47:54,276
five, six, seven, eight,

1256
00:47:54,277 --> 00:47:57,086
nine, ten. Nineteen, twenty, twenty-one, twenty-two.

1257
00:47:57,087 --> 00:47:58,187
Okay, 220 dollars.

1258
00:47:58,747 --> 00:48:00,487
- Nice.
- We must be good at work.

1259
00:48:01,787 --> 00:48:03,327
The math checks out.

1260
00:48:04,127 --> 00:48:06,457
Shall we move on to the corn field?

1261
00:48:07,127 --> 00:48:08,196
(Absolutely!)

1262
00:48:08,197 --> 00:48:09,266
- Oh, my.
- Oh, dear.

1263
00:48:09,267 --> 00:48:10,396
It was tough, you know?

1264
00:48:10,397 --> 00:48:11,866
- Did you harvest many peppers?
- Yes.

1265
00:48:11,867 --> 00:48:13,996
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1266
00:48:13,997 --> 00:48:15,366
- They look tasty.
- There are pepper leaves.

1267
00:48:15,367 --> 00:48:16,637
Make them into a side dish.

1268
00:48:16,807 --> 00:48:18,436
- It's not much.
- We picked 55kg.

1269
00:48:18,437 --> 00:48:19,607
You worked hard.

1270
00:48:20,377 --> 00:48:21,377
Good.

1271
00:48:21,378 --> 00:48:23,246
- We'll enjoy them.
- Thank you.

1272
00:48:23,247 --> 00:48:25,077
- Thank you.
- We'll enjoy the peppers.

1273
00:48:26,947 --> 00:48:29,417
(The peppers the siblings worked hard to harvest today)

1274
00:48:30,447 --> 00:48:33,457
(Soaking up Yeosu's warm sunshine)

1275
00:48:35,987 --> 00:48:37,627
(After being processed in various forms)

1276
00:48:41,097 --> 00:48:42,897
(Pepper makes our meals even more delicious.)

1277
00:48:44,527 --> 00:48:46,566
(Korea's red flavour, chilli peppers)

1278
