- I will... You're fast.
- Sun Young.

1779
01:08:29,574 --> 01:08:30,574
I was going to go.

1780
01:08:30,575 --> 01:08:32,813
(A delivery service for Sun Young who's seated far away to cook)

1781
01:08:32,814 --> 01:08:34,183
It tastes good plain.

1782
01:08:34,184 --> 01:08:35,784
(He blows it to cool it down.)

1783
01:08:36,344 --> 01:08:38,784
(Straight into her mouth)

1784
01:08:40,054 --> 01:08:42,524
(Her eyes open wide.)

1785
01:08:42,584 --> 01:08:43,724
You know,

1786
01:08:44,094 --> 01:08:47,194
I smell some scent from the jeon. What scent is it?

1787
01:08:47,764 --> 01:08:50,764
- You're right.
- It smells like flower...

1788
01:08:50,864 --> 01:08:53,063
- Oh, it's potato scent.
- Potatoes must have a scent too.

1789
01:08:53,064 --> 01:08:54,064
Potato scent.

1790
01:08:54,264 --> 01:08:55,603
- Potatoes have a scent.
- The potatoes...

1791
01:08:55,604 --> 01:08:57,280
- were really high quality.
- Shredded potatoes...

1792
01:08:57,304 --> 01:09:00,673
have a stronger scent than ground ones.

1793
01:09:00,674 --> 01:09:02,004
It's fragrant.

1794
01:09:03,944 --> 01:09:05,073
The potatoes are tasty.

1795
01:09:05,074 --> 01:09:07,714
(Containing all the fragrance of the potatoes which are in season)

1796
01:09:07,844 --> 01:09:09,713
You're supposed to have it with this.

1797
01:09:09,714 --> 01:09:10,953
- Really?
- Yes.

1798
01:09:10,954 --> 01:09:13,053
(Freshly-cooked potato jeon's humble yet addictive taste)

1799
01:09:13,054 --> 01:09:14,054
It's so good.

1800
01:09:14,554 --> 01:09:16,884
(Next, they try pickled onions and smoked duck.)

1801
01:09:17,094 --> 01:09:18,254
It's tasty.

1802
01:09:20,424 --> 01:09:23,933
(Jung Ah places sweet and sour pickled onions on lean duck.)

1803
01:09:23,934 --> 01:09:25,174
- It's so good.
- It's so good.

1804
01:09:27,204 --> 01:09:29,534
(Chewy and crunchy)

1805
01:09:30,364 --> 01:09:32,974
(The tasty food makes her smile.)

1806
01:09:33,534 --> 01:09:35,943
This is interesting too. Potatoes and onions...

1807
01:09:35,944 --> 01:09:37,473
(Potato jeon smell fills the air, and delicious food fills the table.)

1808
01:09:37,474 --> 01:09:38,774
They're the same.

1809
01:09:40,014 --> 01:09:46,714
(Happy snack time)

1810
01:09:47,014 --> 01:09:48,984
Where did you study cooking, Doctor?

1811
01:09:49,754 --> 01:09:51,894
- I was in the States for a bit.
- In the States?

1812
01:09:52,324 --> 01:09:53,994
Is this American potato jeon?

1813
01:09:54,094 --> 01:09:56,194
- Yes, well, it's French Fries.
- French Fries?

1814
01:09:57,234 --> 01:09:59,764
(Aunt Jennica from the US likes it.)

1815
01:10:00,334 --> 01:10:01,363
I see.

1816
01:10:01,364 --> 01:10:03,304
(The cooking master studied in the US.)

1817
01:10:03,704 --> 01:10:06,034
- She's started to make a big one.
- This is the last one.

1818
01:10:07,074 --> 01:10:09,044
(Golden brown)

1819
01:10:09,504 --> 01:10:11,214
(This is the last potato jeon.)

1820
01:10:12,444 --> 01:10:13,813
It looks so good.

1821
01:10:13,814 --> 01:10:16,184
(Flipping the last potato jeon)

1822
01:10:16,444 --> 01:10:17,454
Yes!

1823
01:10:17,554 --> 01:10:18,613
(Cheering)

1824
01:10:18,614 --> 01:10:19,654
(Feeling proud)

1825
01:10:20,084 --> 01:10:21,624
Oh, my gosh.

1826
01:10:22,384 --> 01:10:24,453
Ever since she's made...

1827
01:10:24,454 --> 01:10:26,523
hundreds of jeons for the elderly last time,

1828
01:10:26,524 --> 01:10:28,423
- she's become...
- She's the goddess of jeon.

1829
01:10:28,424 --> 01:10:30,763
- a jeon master.
- I've been good at it since before.

1830
01:10:30,764 --> 01:10:32,740
(Master Kim Jeon Young has become the goddess of jeon.)

1831
01:10:32,764 --> 01:10:36,004
Here comes the next one.

1832
01:10:36,634 --> 01:10:39,434
(Freshly-cooked hot potato jeon)

1833
01:10:40,404 --> 01:10:46,674
(They fill up their stomachs with delicious food...)

1834
01:10:47,684 --> 01:10:51,714
(and relieve today's fatigue.)

1835
01:10:52,054 --> 01:10:53,113
It's nice.

1836
01:10:53,114 --> 01:10:55,654
(The siblings spend a relaxing afternoon.)

1837
01:10:56,154 --> 01:10:57,754
When will we draw the mural?

1838
01:10:58,154 --> 01:11:00,154
(What mural?)

1839
01:11:00,524 --> 01:11:03,323
This wall? Is it the one in front?

1840
01:11:03,324 --> 01:11:04,594
(What are they talking about?)

1841
01:11:04,894 --> 01:11:07,364
(The story started a month ago.)

1842
01:11:07,764 --> 01:11:09,164
- This time, - Yes.

1843
01:11:09,434 --> 01:11:11,773
Why don't we draw a mural?

1844
01:11:11,774 --> 01:11:13,204
Decorate the village and so on.

1845
01:11:13,904 --> 01:11:15,203
You must get the permission of the villagers.

1846
01:11:15,204 --> 01:11:16,274
We will.

1847
01:11:16,674 --> 01:11:19,473
Some of the villages we went had really pretty murals.

1848
01:11:19,474 --> 01:11:21,444
- Hadong had them.
- Hadong, yes.

1849
01:11:22,214 --> 01:11:23,813
The first place had murals too.

1850
01:11:23,814 --> 01:11:25,083
(They welcomed the siblings with open arms.)

1851
01:11:25,084 --> 01:11:27,524
- Murals were really nice.
- They were.

1852
01:11:28,024 --> 01:11:29,253
I'm really bad at drawing.

1853
01:11:29,254 --> 01:11:30,483
- Sun Young and you...
- I'm bad at it too.

1854
01:11:30,484 --> 01:11:33,354
- She can draw, and we can paint.
- I'm bad at painting too.

1855
01:11:33,554 --> 01:11:35,994
- You can draw.
- Painting is easy.

1856
01:11:36,694 --> 01:11:40,334
There was a time when I only drew. Nowadays, not so much.

1857
01:11:40,604 --> 01:11:41,604
I draw anything and everything.

1858
01:11:41,605 --> 01:11:44,204
There's a limit to how well I can draw.

1859
01:11:44,774 --> 01:11:46,633
This is my favourite among the recent ones,

1860
01:11:46,634 --> 01:11:47,874
so I hung it in my living room.

1861
01:11:48,244 --> 01:11:50,003
I just wing it.

1862
01:11:50,004 --> 01:11:51,450
(Jung Ah knew about Sun Young's passion for drawing.)

1863
01:11:51,474 --> 01:11:53,074
I have so many things I want to draw,

1864
01:11:53,174 --> 01:11:55,084
but I don't know how.

1865
01:11:55,644 --> 01:11:57,954
Yoon Seo must be able to do it all since she learned how.

1866
01:11:58,084 --> 01:11:59,813
Why would we need to draw there anyway?

1867
01:11:59,814 --> 01:12:01,854
(Right on point)

1868
01:12:02,084 --> 01:12:03,964
We ask what kind of style the villagers want...

1869
01:12:04,324 --> 01:12:05,630
and decorate the village accordingly.

1870
01:12:05,654 --> 01:12:08,394
It sounds amazing. We can do it while Yoon Seo is here.

1871
01:12:08,494 --> 01:12:09,763
Let's make full use of her.

1872
01:12:09,764 --> 01:12:11,164
(Make full use of the art student.)

1873
01:12:12,894 --> 01:12:15,604
(The art student is full of worries.)

1874
01:12:15,964 --> 01:12:18,934
Will you paint the background before drawing?

1875
01:12:19,474 --> 01:12:21,744
I need to check the wall first.

1876
01:12:22,244 --> 01:12:24,744
(Where Yoon Seo pointed...)

1877
01:12:26,814 --> 01:12:30,084
(has murals lined up next to the breakwater.)

1878
01:12:30,614 --> 01:12:34,554
(From a cute mural of sea creatures swimming...)

1879
01:12:35,084 --> 01:12:39,224
(to a mural with the lives of the fishing village)

1880
01:12:39,454 --> 01:12:41,964
I hear there's an empty spot on the wall.

1881
01:12:42,594 --> 01:12:44,363
They're lending it to us?

1882
01:12:44,364 --> 01:12:46,793
Yes. There so happens to be one empty spot.

1883
01:12:46,794 --> 01:12:48,903
It'll be nice to fill it up.

1884
01:12:48,904 --> 01:12:51,974
- The villagers would like it.
- We'll do it tomorrow afternoon.

1885
01:12:52,274 --> 01:12:53,533
Shall we go?

1886
01:12:53,534 --> 01:12:55,650
(Let's go to the wall where the siblings will paint on.)

1887
01:12:55,674 --> 01:12:56,743
A mural.

1888
01:12:56,744 --> 01:12:57,774
(Excited and nervous)

1889
01:12:57,874 --> 01:12:59,674
Which way should we go?

1890
01:13:00,444 --> 01:13:02,213
- It's really pretty.
- The stones...

1891
01:13:02,214 --> 01:13:03,243
(They explore the village as they walk.)

1892
01:13:03,244 --> 01:13:04,284
They're pretty.

1893
01:13:05,154 --> 01:13:08,354
(Various colours blend in together to create a warm atmosphere.)

1894
01:13:08,584 --> 01:13:09,954
That's the spot.

1895
01:13:10,654 --> 01:13:13,094
- The wall is pretty long.
- It's wide.

1896
01:13:14,294 --> 01:13:15,523
- That's...
- An hour or two won't cut it.

1897
01:13:15,524 --> 01:13:16,763
- It won't.
- This is practically work.

1898
01:13:16,764 --> 01:13:17,764
Exactly.

1899
01:13:17,864 --> 01:13:20,833
(That's a huge wall.)

1900
01:13:20,834 --> 01:13:21,834
It's big.

1901
01:13:22,064 --> 01:13:23,103
This...

1902
01:13:23,104 --> 01:13:24,833
(It makes the siblings look like figures.)

1903
01:13:24,834 --> 01:13:25,904
Goodness.

1904
01:13:26,404 --> 01:13:29,204
(This wall is 13 by 1.5 meters.)

1905
01:13:30,174 --> 01:13:32,044
(To estimate the size...)

1906
01:13:32,244 --> 01:13:34,814
(A canvas as big as a grown woman, 150 by 110 centimetres)

1907
01:13:37,214 --> 01:13:40,454
(12 such canvases can fit.)

1908
01:13:40,854 --> 01:13:42,454
When will we finish this?

1909
01:13:42,754 --> 01:13:45,454
Should we sketch it today?

1910
01:13:46,054 --> 01:13:48,794
- They even coloured the background.
- Goodness.

1911
01:13:49,824 --> 01:13:51,893
(Next to the siblings' wall, )

1912
01:13:51,894 --> 01:13:54,764
(a mural is already in place.)

1913
01:13:56,304 --> 01:13:58,173
- Is it possible?
- I have no idea.

1914
01:13:58,174 --> 01:13:59,310
(Although the colours have faded, there are five background colours.)

1915
01:13:59,334 --> 01:14:00,374
But...

1916
01:14:01,004 --> 01:14:02,544
if we're drawing at this level,

1917
01:14:03,274 --> 01:14:04,873
- it can be done quickly.
- It'll be fast.

1918
01:14:04,874 --> 01:14:05,943
- Really?
- Yes.

1919
01:14:05,944 --> 01:14:08,513
- This won't take so long.
- It won't.

1920
01:14:08,514 --> 01:14:09,514
Really?

1921
01:14:09,984 --> 01:14:12,013
We shouldn't draw something so detailed.

1922
01:14:12,014 --> 01:14:14,484
Exactly. Draw them big.

1923
01:14:15,384 --> 01:14:16,854
- Like this.
- Yes.

1924
01:14:17,254 --> 01:14:18,254
With seaweed?

1925
01:14:18,354 --> 01:14:19,423
Just this.

1926
01:14:19,424 --> 01:14:21,124
(They aren't thugs.)

1927
01:14:21,224 --> 01:14:23,964
I think we should draw something...

1928
01:14:24,234 --> 01:14:26,264
in continuation of this mural.

1929
01:14:27,264 --> 01:14:30,133
We should connect the waves.

1930
01:14:30,134 --> 01:14:31,704
Yes, the sea.

1931
01:14:32,104 --> 01:14:34,403
We'll paint it in a way...

1932
01:14:34,404 --> 01:14:36,703
that looks similar to the faded painting.

1933
01:14:36,704 --> 01:14:38,544
That boat looks nice.

1934
01:14:39,344 --> 01:14:42,584
- A boat... Right.
- I'll draw a boat.

1935
01:14:43,144 --> 01:14:46,713
Let's draw dolphins and a few fish.

1936
01:14:46,714 --> 01:14:49,554
Sun Young, sketch the fish.

1937
01:14:49,924 --> 01:14:52,294
Sang Hun, you can draw an octopus or something, right?

1938
01:14:52,524 --> 01:14:54,023
Yes, I can.

1939
01:14:54,024 --> 01:14:55,624
Just this level.

1940
01:14:56,424 --> 01:14:59,734
(The siblings will draw the mural to form one sea.)

1941
01:15:00,034 --> 01:15:01,734
I'll draw the waves first.

1942
01:15:01,764 --> 01:15:03,834
We'll paint the background first and let it dry.

1943
01:15:04,334 --> 01:15:07,574
We'll draw the boat and so on tomorrow.

1944
01:15:08,644 --> 01:15:10,913
Today, Sang Hun and I will cook.

1945
01:15:10,914 --> 01:15:12,914
- You guys...
- Okay.

1946
01:15:13,314 --> 01:15:15,313
Sang Hun and I will cook.

1947
01:15:15,314 --> 01:15:17,114
You guys work on the mural here.

1948
01:15:17,514 --> 01:15:19,554
We'll paint the background.

1949
01:15:19,984 --> 01:15:23,453
Tomorrow, we'll all come and paint on top of it tomorrow.

1950
01:15:23,454 --> 01:15:24,753
Yes, it needs to dry.

1951
01:15:24,754 --> 01:15:26,994
Let's start something today.

1952
01:15:28,394 --> 01:15:30,524
I'm grateful.

1953
01:15:31,164 --> 01:15:34,234
We don't need to use black like them for the waves.

1954
01:15:34,564 --> 01:15:35,763
- What should I do?
- The waves...

1955
01:15:35,764 --> 01:15:36,764
- Differently?
- Yes.

1956
01:15:36,765 --> 01:15:39,103
Pick three cool colours.

1957
01:15:39,104 --> 01:15:41,473
Then I'll paint a gradient at the end.

1958
01:15:41,474 --> 01:15:42,504
(More serious than ever)

1959
01:15:44,104 --> 01:15:47,544
(What will this wall turn into?)

1960
01:15:48,214 --> 01:15:50,283
It's my first time doing work on such a big scale.

1961
01:15:50,284 --> 01:15:51,883
(Filling up the wide wall)

1962
01:15:51,884 --> 01:15:53,113
That's such a nice colour.

1963
01:15:53,114 --> 01:15:54,284
(The siblings' hands)

1964
01:15:54,584 --> 01:15:56,724
It uses up a lot of your energy.

1965
01:15:56,854 --> 01:15:58,524
Did you all learn art?

1966
01:16:00,024 --> 01:16:05,134
(Fresh off the Sea, their mural-painting challenge)

1967
01:16:05,634 --> 01:16:07,193
Let me check the draft.

1968
01:16:07,194 --> 01:16:08,303
(Time to prepare before painting on the wall)

1969
01:16:08,304 --> 01:16:09,304
The draft...

1970
01:16:09,364 --> 01:16:10,364
(Yoon Seo is coming up with a draft.)

1971
01:16:10,365 --> 01:16:13,203
I've never drawn ever since I've graduated.

1972
01:16:13,204 --> 01:16:16,773
I never drew. Don't expect so much from me.

1973
01:16:16,774 --> 01:16:18,213
This is so hard for me too.

1974
01:16:18,214 --> 01:16:20,573
I'm not an illustrator. I studied fine art.

1975
01:16:20,574 --> 01:16:22,284
I've never drawn an illustration.

1976
01:16:22,544 --> 01:16:25,013
Poor Yoon Seo.

1977
01:16:25,014 --> 01:16:26,014
(They're holding back their laughter because Yoon Seo is so cute.)

1978
01:16:26,015 --> 01:16:28,623
I feel so pressured when I think about how it'd last forever.

1979
01:16:28,624 --> 01:16:30,400
(The more she wants to do well, the more pressured she feels.)

1980
01:16:30,424 --> 01:16:33,953
(She still checks the draft while she's stressed.)

1981
01:16:33,954 --> 01:16:35,294
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

1982
01:16:35,764 --> 01:16:36,893
This will be fun.

1983
01:16:36,894 --> 01:16:38,310
(No more worrying, let's get going.)

1984
01:16:38,334 --> 01:16:39,334
(Walking)

1985
01:16:39,334 --> 01:16:40,334
- Doctor.
- Yes?

1986
01:16:40,335 --> 01:16:41,433
Good luck.

1987
01:16:41,434 --> 01:16:43,404
- We'll get going.
- We'll go and do some art.

1988
01:16:43,834 --> 01:16:46,433
- You know, art...
- Yes.

1989
01:16:46,434 --> 01:16:48,234
(Doctor Jeong Sang Hun's introduction to art)

1990
01:16:48,604 --> 01:16:50,574
I don't know what you think about it,

1991
01:16:50,914 --> 01:16:52,543
but you shouldn't take it lightly.

1992
01:16:52,544 --> 01:16:53,544
- Okay.
- Okay.

1993
01:16:54,944 --> 01:16:56,114
I'm not done talking.

1994
01:16:56,984 --> 01:16:59,414
I'm not done talking. Don't leave.

1995
01:16:59,984 --> 01:17:01,783
What you're thinking,

1996
01:17:01,784 --> 01:17:03,523
- Beyond...
- and what you insist on.

1997
01:17:03,524 --> 01:17:05,094
- Yes.
- Get rid of those thoughts.

1998
01:17:05,854 --> 01:17:07,254
- That's not it.
- Get rid of them?

1999
01:17:07,324 --> 01:17:09,593
I was about to bring those thoughts with me.

2000
01:17:09,594 --> 01:17:11,634
- Don't. Get rid of them.
- Get rid of them? Okay.

2001
01:17:12,094 --> 01:17:14,433
At times, you need to listen to those younger than you.

2002
01:17:14,434 --> 01:17:15,963
Of course.

2003
01:17:15,964 --> 01:17:17,004
And...

2004
01:17:17,434 --> 01:17:19,433
we shouldn't take responsibility.

2005
01:17:19,434 --> 01:17:20,503
(Part 3. Don't take responsibility.)

2006
01:17:20,504 --> 01:17:22,473
- If possible...
- Avoiding responsibility?

2007
01:17:22,474 --> 01:17:24,613
- If possible, don't take...
- Avoid responsibility?

2008
01:17:24,614 --> 01:17:26,443
- That's such an important point.
- Exactly.

2009
01:17:26,444 --> 01:17:27,913
- As expected.
- As expected from a doctor.

2010
01:17:27,914 --> 01:17:29,513
An American doctor is different.

2011
01:17:29,514 --> 01:17:30,843
- He's from the US?
- I understand.

2012
01:17:30,844 --> 01:17:32,453
- I'll get going.
- Take it easy.

2013
01:17:32,454 --> 01:17:33,583
- I will. I won't take...
- See you.

2014
01:17:33,584 --> 01:17:34,753
Any responsibility.

2015
01:17:34,754 --> 01:17:36,684
- See you.
- Just breathe loudly.

2016
01:17:36,854 --> 01:17:38,254
We're off to do some art.

2017
01:17:38,954 --> 01:17:40,623
I won't take any responsibility.

2018
01:17:40,624 --> 01:17:42,924
(The mural expedition leaves with a firm resolve.)

2019
01:17:43,264 --> 01:17:44,264
It's going to be so fun.

2020
01:17:44,265 --> 01:17:46,263
I can't believe I'm drawing on this show.

2021
01:17:46,264 --> 01:17:47,264
Me too.

2022
01:17:47,265 --> 01:17:48,785
This is so much more fun than cooking.

2023
01:17:50,264 --> 01:17:51,274
It's fun.

2024
01:17:51,934 --> 01:17:53,973
I really like looking at different colours.

2025
01:17:53,974 --> 01:17:56,174
- Right? So I...
- Yes, making colours.

2026
01:17:56,274 --> 01:17:58,373
Whenever I go to an art store, I want to buy...

2027
01:17:58,374 --> 01:17:59,643
every pretty colour.

2028
01:17:59,644 --> 01:18:00,984
Have you ever drawn?

2029
01:18:01,384 --> 01:18:04,454
I'm a complete stranger to it.

2030
01:18:04,714 --> 01:18:06,613
(I hope you two become close today.)

2031
01:18:06,614 --> 01:18:07,823
Why am I nervous?

2032
01:18:07,824 --> 01:18:09,600
(On the other hand, Sun Young can't stop smiling.)

2033
01:18:09,624 --> 01:18:11,754
I like this 100 times more than cooking.

2034
01:18:12,894 --> 01:18:14,253
Me too. I'm 100 times more useful.

2035
01:18:14,254 --> 01:18:16,194
I get to enjoy the luxury.

2036
01:18:17,224 --> 01:18:19,734
Contemporary art changes depending on how you interpret it.

2037
01:18:20,664 --> 01:18:23,364
I'm thinking of quitting my job and becoming a painter.

2038
01:18:24,374 --> 01:18:25,534
I'm detailed.

2039
01:18:25,804 --> 01:18:27,434
I'll pour my soul into my art.

2040
01:18:27,874 --> 01:18:28,973
(Today's mural plan)

2041
01:18:28,974 --> 01:18:32,173
Yoon Seo, do an overall sketch of the waves.

2042
01:18:32,174 --> 01:18:33,390
(1. Draw the sketch of the waves. 2. Colour the background.)

2043
01:18:33,414 --> 01:18:35,183
(Painter Roh will do the sketch.)

2044
01:18:35,184 --> 01:18:36,683
That's fascinating. What is it?

2045
01:18:36,684 --> 01:18:37,814
- A chalk.
- A chalk.

2046
01:18:38,014 --> 01:18:39,384
- That's a chalk?
- Yes.

2047
01:18:40,384 --> 01:18:41,983
- Here.
- I guess you draw the sketch...

2048
01:18:41,984 --> 01:18:42,984
with a chalk.

2049
01:18:43,784 --> 01:18:47,154
Four... One, two, three, four. Okay.

2050
01:18:47,794 --> 01:18:49,524
- I'll just draw.
- Yes.

2051
01:18:50,264 --> 01:18:52,334
(She goes straight to the wall without hesitation.)

2052
01:18:52,794 --> 01:18:54,833
(She takes a glance...)

2053
01:18:54,834 --> 01:18:57,504
(and starts drawing.)

2054
01:18:57,674 --> 01:18:59,733
(She glances...)

2055
01:18:59,734 --> 01:19:01,904
(and draws.)

2056
01:19:02,274 --> 01:19:04,104
(She's pretty good.)

2057
01:19:04,744 --> 01:19:06,113
(The time taken for her to reach the middle of the 13m-width wall)

2058
01:19:06,114 --> 01:19:08,144
(Only 30 seconds)

2059
01:19:09,544 --> 01:19:10,684
Okay.

2060
01:19:11,284 --> 01:19:13,553
(Walking proudly)

2061
01:19:13,554 --> 01:19:14,723
You Seok, pass me a white chalk.

2062
01:19:14,724 --> 01:19:16,330
(You Seok, as thoughtful as ever, has the next chalk ready.)

2063
01:19:16,354 --> 01:19:19,124
(She draws the remaining part faster!)

2064
01:19:19,554 --> 01:19:21,163
(Sun Young and You Seok open the paints first.)

2065
01:19:21,164 --> 01:19:22,994
- Yellow.
- White.

2066
01:19:23,564 --> 01:19:25,164
It smells so nice.

2067
01:19:25,194 --> 01:19:26,564
- Does it?
- Yes.

2068
01:19:28,204 --> 01:19:32,304
(Waves are created with each stroke.)

2069
01:19:33,404 --> 01:19:34,404
I'm done with the sketch.

2070
01:19:35,144 --> 01:19:39,944
(The waves sketch is complete in the blink of an eye!)

2071
01:19:40,544 --> 01:19:42,383
How will you colour it?

2072
01:19:42,384 --> 01:19:43,620
(2. Paint the background and let it dry.)

2073
01:19:43,644 --> 01:19:45,254
Let's mix the paints.

2074
01:19:46,654 --> 01:19:48,183
(You can create the colour you want by mixing the paints.)

2075
01:19:48,184 --> 01:19:49,853
(Normally, you use 3 to 5 basic colours.)

2076
01:19:49,854 --> 01:19:51,993
- We'll mix the paints here...
- Okay.

2077
01:19:51,994 --> 01:19:53,354
And colour the wall using rollers.

2078
01:19:53,494 --> 01:19:55,764
Tell me what to do. Where should I pour it?

2079
01:19:56,094 --> 01:19:57,424
- Here?
- Stop.

2080
01:19:58,234 --> 01:20:00,264
- Do I mix it?
- A bit of white. Stop.

2081
01:20:01,504 --> 01:20:03,333
(Depending on the ratio of the mix, the colour changes completely.)

2082
01:20:03,334 --> 01:20:04,903
- I'll look nice to paint like this.
- Exactly.

2083
01:20:04,904 --> 01:20:05,904
It...

2084
01:20:06,774 --> 01:20:08,304
It has a gradient.

2085
01:20:09,274 --> 01:20:10,603
Like this.

2086
01:20:10,604 --> 01:20:12,214
It's pretty. I love it.

2087
01:20:12,974 --> 01:20:14,843
- Without mixing them.
- It's pretty.

2088
01:20:14,844 --> 01:20:17,443
I like this. It looks like real waves.

2089
01:20:17,444 --> 01:20:18,453
(Like white foams on the blue sea)

2090
01:20:18,454 --> 01:20:19,514
It's so pretty.

2091
01:20:20,054 --> 01:20:22,324
This shouldn't take long. I'll do it.

2092
01:20:22,624 --> 01:20:24,923
Okay. Bring me the big one.

2093
01:20:24,924 --> 01:20:26,330
I'll make the colour for the wave on top.

2094
01:20:26,354 --> 01:20:28,363
You can use both the brush and the roller.

2095
01:20:28,364 --> 01:20:29,524
I'll be really quick.

2096
01:20:30,664 --> 01:20:32,293
(She paints excitedly following the wave sketch.)

2097
01:20:32,294 --> 01:20:33,334
I'm excited.

2098
01:20:33,934 --> 01:20:36,603
This is so fun.

2099
01:20:36,604 --> 01:20:38,533
(My own sea)

2100
01:20:38,534 --> 01:20:40,134
This is so fun.

2101
01:20:42,044 --> 01:20:45,014
It's been so long. I'm so excited.

2102
01:20:45,844 --> 01:20:48,214
(Sun Young is on a roll.)

2103
01:20:48,984 --> 01:20:50,843
Can you fill up the empty spots?

2104
01:20:50,844 --> 01:20:52,604
- I'll paint there again after this.
- Okay.

2105
01:20:53,284 --> 01:20:55,423
(Empty patches)

2106
01:20:55,424 --> 01:20:56,424
(Grunting)

2107
01:20:56,454 --> 01:20:58,454
(The path to an artist isn't easy.)

2108
01:20:58,924 --> 01:21:00,853
I'll be bold and add more.

2109
01:21:00,854 --> 01:21:01,923
(Meanwhile, to the blue paint, which will serve as the base)

2110
01:21:01,924 --> 01:21:04,023
- What colour are you making?
- Cyan.

2111
01:21:04,024 --> 01:21:05,193
Cyan?

2112
01:21:05,194 --> 01:21:07,933
Can you use this to paint the second wave?

2113
01:21:07,934 --> 01:21:09,663
Will do. It's going to be fun.

2114
01:21:09,664 --> 01:21:11,174
(Kang Vinci gets to work too.)

2115
01:21:11,804 --> 01:21:14,274
(He carefully makes his first stroke.)

2116
01:21:14,774 --> 01:21:16,304
- It's fun, right?
- It is.

2117
01:21:16,404 --> 01:21:17,964
It's like I'm colouring a colouring book.

2118
01:21:19,314 --> 01:21:20,474
You're good at it.

2119
01:21:21,284 --> 01:21:22,644
Painting is easy.

2120
01:21:23,484 --> 01:21:25,354
(He's doing well.)

2121
01:21:25,854 --> 01:21:27,283
(Yoon Seo finishes mixing the third colour...)

2122
01:21:27,284 --> 01:21:28,724
(and starts painting.)

2123
01:21:29,424 --> 01:21:31,083
(Although she mixed the same colours, the resulting colour is different!)

2124
01:21:31,084 --> 01:21:32,424
I'm sweating.

2125
01:21:33,824 --> 01:21:35,963
(With their own blue, )

2126
01:21:35,964 --> 01:21:39,764
(they're colouring the waves.)

2127
01:21:40,094 --> 01:21:41,164
This is so fun.

2128
01:21:41,334 --> 01:21:43,134
Let me retouch it now.

2129
01:21:43,834 --> 01:21:45,933
- It'll be finished soon, right?
- Yes.

2130
01:21:45,934 --> 01:21:48,294
(After 1 hour of painting, the wall is filled with colours.)

2131
01:21:49,804 --> 01:21:53,344
(Meanwhile, Sun Young, who was quietly staring at the wall...)

2132
01:21:53,474 --> 01:21:55,283
- You know what, Yoon Seo?
- Yes?

2133
01:21:55,284 --> 01:21:57,114
Let's paint over this.

2134
01:21:58,084 --> 01:21:59,084
This...

2135
01:21:59,114 --> 01:22:00,783
Let's paint over this.

2136
01:22:00,784 --> 01:22:03,060
(She suddenly suggests to paint over what they've been doing?)

2137
01:22:03,084 --> 01:22:05,394
We went a bit insane with colours for a while.

2138
01:22:06,154 --> 01:22:09,093
The colours are too similar, so this doesn't stand out...

2139
01:22:09,094 --> 01:22:10,463
- from afar.
- Right? They're too...

2140
01:22:10,464 --> 01:22:11,594
This doesn't stand out.

2141
01:22:11,794 --> 01:22:14,863
(They're supposed to be different waves.)

2142
01:22:14,864 --> 01:22:17,233
Because there's green,

2143
01:22:17,234 --> 01:22:18,774
it could look like a mountain.

2144
01:22:19,904 --> 01:22:23,443
- Gosh, this is so pretty!
- Right?

2145
01:22:23,444 --> 01:22:26,173
- I want to use it as is.
- Me too.

2146
01:22:26,174 --> 01:22:28,414
- We should use one colour.
- Should I mix them?

2147
01:22:29,614 --> 01:22:31,144
Were we too ambitious?

2148
01:22:32,154 --> 01:22:34,524
It's okay. We pursued our dreams.

2149
01:22:35,284 --> 01:22:37,923
- Nice.
- Yes, that's it.

2150
01:22:37,924 --> 01:22:39,153
(They cheer each other on and pick up the pace.)

2151
01:22:39,154 --> 01:22:40,553
That's nice. Keep it up.

2152
01:22:40,554 --> 01:22:43,094
(You just need to paint it over!)

2153
01:22:43,394 --> 01:22:44,834
The sun is too strong.

2154
01:22:44,994 --> 01:22:46,133
Exactly.

2155
01:22:46,134 --> 01:22:48,610
(They've been working for 1 hour under the hot sun over 30°C.)

2156
01:22:48,634 --> 01:22:50,633
(But none of them show their struggles.)

2157
01:22:50,634 --> 01:22:53,434
(The three siblings do their best.)

2158
01:22:53,874 --> 01:22:56,174
We should show this to Jung Ah and Sang Hun later.

2159
01:22:59,114 --> 01:23:02,744
(They pick up the pace excitedly.)

2160
01:23:03,384 --> 01:23:07,484
(The summer sun hangs on the rocky mountain.)

2161
01:23:08,584 --> 01:23:12,354
(It's evening in Seongdu Village.)

2162
01:23:13,624 --> 01:23:16,294
(Kim Hwa Yeob's home)

2163
01:23:17,064 --> 01:23:20,264
I used fresh Yeosu gizzard shad.

2164
01:23:21,034 --> 01:23:22,203
I use a lot.

2165
01:23:22,204 --> 01:23:23,533
(Another handful of raw gizzard shad!)

2166
01:23:23,534 --> 01:23:25,534
Slice radish...

2167
01:23:25,634 --> 01:23:26,994
and put it in with perilla leaves.

2168
01:23:27,574 --> 01:23:29,373
And add some peppers.

2169
01:23:29,374 --> 01:23:30,374
(And the red flavour?)

2170
01:23:30,374 --> 01:23:31,374
Red peppers.

2171
01:23:31,375 --> 01:23:33,374
(Yeosu red peppers!)

2172
01:23:33,714 --> 01:23:34,843
Chojang.

2173
01:23:34,844 --> 01:23:36,513
(Put spicy and sweet chojang on it.)

2174
01:23:36,514 --> 01:23:37,643
Mix them.

2175
01:23:37,644 --> 01:23:39,554
(Mix them well.)

2176
01:23:39,714 --> 01:23:41,483
It's seasoned raw gizzard shad.

2177
01:23:41,484 --> 01:23:44,083
(Yeosu seasoned raw gizzard shad)

2178
01:23:44,084 --> 01:23:46,593
And in summer,

2179
01:23:46,594 --> 01:23:50,394
I add various fruits and vegetables.

2180
01:23:50,894 --> 01:23:53,333
I picked the loquats and made it myself.

2181
01:23:53,334 --> 01:23:55,434
(Add handmade loquat syrup.)

2182
01:23:56,064 --> 01:23:57,064
Add water.

2183
01:23:57,065 --> 01:23:58,204
(Add cold water.)

2184
01:23:59,304 --> 01:24:00,903
It's cold cucumber soup.

2185
01:24:00,904 --> 01:24:02,584
(Sloshing cold cucumber soup is complete!)

2186
01:24:02,774 --> 01:24:05,343
(What is summer known for?)

2187
01:24:05,344 --> 01:24:07,743
My neighbour grew these themselves.

2188
01:24:07,744 --> 01:24:08,784
(Corns, of course!)

2189
01:24:09,884 --> 01:24:11,183
Add the kernels.

2190
01:24:11,184 --> 01:24:12,184
(Pan-fried chewy kernels)

2191
01:24:12,654 --> 01:24:14,113
It's corn jeon.

2192
01:24:14,114 --> 01:24:16,354
(Chewy and savoury corn jeon!)

2193
01:24:17,754 --> 01:24:19,323
(A colourful dinner of Yeosu's summer)

2194
01:24:19,324 --> 01:24:20,953
(Seasoned raw gizzard shad, bitter lettuce kimchi, corn jeon, )

2195
01:24:20,954 --> 01:24:23,154
(purple rice with beans, red pepper cold cucumber soup)

2196
01:24:23,964 --> 01:24:26,063
(What are the siblings' first dinner back in Yeosu?)

2197
01:24:26,064 --> 01:24:27,664
Two of us will cook whatever for dinner.

2198
01:24:28,204 --> 01:24:30,963
Tell me what you need, and I'll prepare the ingredients.

2199
01:24:30,964 --> 01:24:33,603
It's okay, you can be in charge of a dish.

2200
01:24:33,604 --> 01:24:35,403
Just the main dishes.

2201
01:24:35,404 --> 01:24:37,120
(The dinner will have only the main dishes?)

2202
01:24:37,144 --> 01:24:38,214
Dried radish leaf soup.

2203
01:24:38,944 --> 01:24:40,274
Ripened kimchi chicken stew.

2204
01:24:40,474 --> 01:24:43,514
I'll use the ripened kimchi the elders in Hadong gave us.

2205
01:24:44,344 --> 01:24:47,513
- Will you make the soup?
- Yes, I'll make the soup.

2206
01:24:47,514 --> 01:24:49,923
I'll boil the chicken first.

2207
01:24:49,924 --> 01:24:51,494
- Let me clean this.
- Give me that.

2208
01:24:51,654 --> 01:24:52,923
Let's prepare the ingredients all at once...

2209
01:24:52,924 --> 01:24:54,964
- and cook everything.
- Right.

2210
01:24:55,764 --> 01:24:58,333
- Bring all the ingredients there...
- Yes.

2211
01:24:58,334 --> 01:25:00,163
And chop everything.

2212
01:25:00,164 --> 01:25:01,194
Okay.

2213
01:25:02,604 --> 01:25:04,973
We should cook rice, right?

2214
01:25:04,974 --> 01:25:05,974
Yes.

2215
01:25:05,975 --> 01:25:07,974
(He's already taking out the rice pot.)

2216
01:25:09,044 --> 01:25:11,043
(Sang Hun takes out the pot smoothly.)

2217
01:25:11,044 --> 01:25:13,774
Where's the rice?

2218
01:25:14,714 --> 01:25:16,144
Check down there.

2219
01:25:16,544 --> 01:25:19,714
(He confidently opens the rice container.)

2220
01:25:20,214 --> 01:25:23,924
(And he gently scoops up the rice.)

2221
01:25:24,654 --> 01:25:26,353
(When he moves it, )

2222
01:25:26,354 --> 01:25:27,854
(he does it cheerfully.)

2223
01:25:28,624 --> 01:25:29,993
Do that first. I'll throw this.

2224
01:25:29,994 --> 01:25:31,540
(He was going to turn on the tab for Jung Ah.)

2225
01:25:31,564 --> 01:25:34,804
(Thanks to Jung Ah, he washes the rice to his heart's content.)

2226
01:25:35,004 --> 01:25:37,303
(With practised ease, )

2227
01:25:37,304 --> 01:25:39,704
(he washes every grain of rice!)

2228
01:25:40,204 --> 01:25:44,974
(Jung Ah was walking past behind him.)

2229
01:25:45,274 --> 01:25:47,414
Can you give me some rice water?

2230
01:25:47,444 --> 01:25:49,643
- Do you want it? Okay.
- I could use it.

2231
01:25:49,644 --> 01:25:50,744
Just a bit of rice water.

2232
01:25:51,114 --> 01:25:52,453
(For Jung Ah who wants to use rice water to cook)

2233
01:25:52,454 --> 01:25:54,613
- Is this enough?
- That's enough.

2234
01:25:54,614 --> 01:25:55,783
I'll put it here.

2235
01:25:55,784 --> 01:25:57,924
(He places rice water in one corner of the kitchen.)

2236
01:25:58,694 --> 01:26:01,694
Let me take out what we'll be using today.

2237
01:26:02,464 --> 01:26:05,164
- Are you going to add beef brisket?
- Yes, I am.

2238
01:26:05,334 --> 01:26:07,363
And mix doenjang and gochujang together.

2239
01:26:07,364 --> 01:26:08,364
- Yes.
- And some garlic.

2240
01:26:08,365 --> 01:26:10,045
- I'll mix doenjang and gochujang.
- Okay.

2241
01:26:10,934 --> 01:26:13,404
(Wrapping up the dishes, wrapping up the table clean up)

2242
01:26:14,134 --> 01:26:18,004
(From the workflow to the recipes, everything flows so smoothly.)

2243
01:26:18,414 --> 01:26:20,814
Why do I move slowly when it's hot?

2244
01:26:21,514 --> 01:26:23,514
- I am slow.
- Yes, you have to move slowly.

2245
01:26:24,514 --> 01:26:26,613
If I move quickly, it's hot.

2246
01:26:26,614 --> 01:26:28,083
(Grabbing)

2247
01:26:28,084 --> 01:26:30,884
(I take it slow, but I don't stop moving.)

2248
01:26:31,324 --> 01:26:33,323
(Nonchalantly...)

2249
01:26:33,324 --> 01:26:36,024
(he gets the rice started.)

2250
01:26:36,464 --> 01:26:39,164
(Jung Ah grabs the ingredients casually too.)

2251
01:26:39,764 --> 01:26:43,334
(Upon seeing that, Sang Hun goes to the fridge.)

2252
01:26:43,964 --> 01:26:46,273
(They look at each other...)

2253
01:26:46,274 --> 01:26:49,074
(and switch over with a turn.)

2254
01:26:49,274 --> 01:26:51,574
I'll use two potatoes.

2255
01:26:51,644 --> 01:26:52,644
Okay.

2256
01:26:52,744 --> 01:26:54,444
- They love potatoes.
- Right.

2257
01:26:57,784 --> 01:27:00,354
(He is fast with the potatoes.)

2258
01:27:00,614 --> 01:27:01,683
(Must-haves for a chicken stew!)

2259
01:27:01,684 --> 01:27:03,160
(He peels the potatoes and carrot mercilessly.)

2260
01:27:03,184 --> 01:27:04,653
(He chops off the top of the onion...)

2261
01:27:04,654 --> 01:27:05,894
(and peels it.)

2262
01:27:06,224 --> 01:27:07,753
(He peels the green onion with bare hands...)

2263
01:27:07,754 --> 01:27:09,524
(and removes the dried part.)

2264
01:27:09,994 --> 01:27:13,434
(The fearless cooking genius prepares the dried radish leaves.)

2265
01:27:13,634 --> 01:27:14,834
(After checking the outside, )

2266
01:27:14,934 --> 01:27:16,563
(he bites and tears open...)

2267
01:27:16,564 --> 01:27:18,474
(the package.)

2268
01:27:19,204 --> 01:27:22,274
(Of course, he rinses the dried radish leaves thoroughly.)

2269
01:27:23,004 --> 01:27:24,043
(He quickly takes the ingredients that need to be chopped outside.)

2270
01:27:24,044 --> 01:27:26,513
- Chop the dried radish leaves.
- I'm going to chop them.

2271
01:27:26,514 --> 01:27:27,814
Yes, I am.

2272
01:27:28,444 --> 01:27:30,543
(Neat and tidy)

2273
01:27:30,544 --> 01:27:31,953
Do I use all of those dried radish leaves?

2274
01:27:31,954 --> 01:27:34,183
Or should I use half of it?

2275
01:27:34,184 --> 01:27:37,184
Am I cooking just for us, or for the staff too?

2276
01:27:37,954 --> 01:27:39,893
When you're on this show, you use everything you have.

2277
01:27:39,894 --> 01:27:40,924
Okay.

2278
01:27:41,594 --> 01:27:43,263
- I'll boil it in a big pot.
- Yes.

2279
01:27:43,264 --> 01:27:44,944
(Sang Hun looks for a big pot right away.)

2280
01:27:45,634 --> 01:27:47,533
They only got small pots over there, right?

2281
01:27:47,534 --> 01:27:48,664
No, there's a big one here.

2282
01:27:49,334 --> 01:27:50,363
This one.

2283
01:27:50,364 --> 01:27:52,533
(Fortunately, he found a big pot.)

2284
01:27:52,534 --> 01:27:54,574
(Relieved)

2285
