01:37:31,284 --> 01:37:34,414
(Wait for a while after adding a bunch of vegetables.)

2533
01:37:35,824 --> 01:37:37,683
(When she opens the lid again...)

2534
01:37:37,684 --> 01:37:40,394
Gosh. The vegetable broth was added.

2535
01:37:41,324 --> 01:37:43,623
(As it boils, the chicken absorbs the sauce deeply.)

2536
01:37:43,624 --> 01:37:45,594
Gosh. Why don't I taste it, then?

2537
01:37:46,394 --> 01:37:47,633
Avengers, assemble.

2538
01:37:47,634 --> 01:37:49,404
(Siblings' Avengers, assemble.)

2539
01:37:49,704 --> 01:37:51,233
- Pepper?
- We can add more pepper.

2540
01:37:51,234 --> 01:37:53,154
(How will the Avenger-level chicken stew taste?)

2541
01:37:53,334 --> 01:37:55,574
The taste of kimchi is strong, isn't it?

2542
01:37:56,404 --> 01:37:57,603
Gosh. It's good.

2543
01:37:57,604 --> 01:37:59,314
(Gosh. It's good.)

2544
01:37:59,644 --> 01:38:02,213
It has a tang like tom yum kung.

2545
01:38:02,214 --> 01:38:05,313
It's a pleasant tang from the ripened kimchi.

2546
01:38:05,314 --> 01:38:06,954
(Sealing it to cook it for the last time)

2547
01:38:07,884 --> 01:38:09,283
(Sang Hun is on the move...)

2548
01:38:09,284 --> 01:38:11,454
(to make the beef brisket and dried radish leaf soup.)

2549
01:38:12,794 --> 01:38:13,824
(Savouring)

2550
01:38:13,924 --> 01:38:15,094
- Do you like it?
- Yes.

2551
01:38:15,724 --> 01:38:17,564
The aroma of the dried radish leaves is great.

2552
01:38:17,994 --> 01:38:19,964
Our Korean food aficionados will love it.

2553
01:38:21,634 --> 01:38:26,074
(Adding the beef briskets into the insane broth)

2554
01:38:26,504 --> 01:38:29,104
(After adding lots of pink beef briskets, )

2555
01:38:30,144 --> 01:38:33,073
(the broth from leaves and the juice from the briskets...)

2556
01:38:33,074 --> 01:38:35,984
(are meld into rich flavours.)

2557
01:38:37,314 --> 01:38:38,513
It's so good.

2558
01:38:38,514 --> 01:38:39,553
(The chicken stew and the soup are coming soon.)

2559
01:38:39,554 --> 01:38:40,584
It's hot.

2560
01:38:40,914 --> 01:38:41,914
It's so hot.

2561
01:38:41,915 --> 01:38:44,523
(She finally stays away from the fire in the midsummer.)

2562
01:38:44,524 --> 01:38:46,554
(If it's hot for me...)

2563
01:38:46,854 --> 01:38:49,364
What about the rest of us? Let me check.

2564
01:38:49,694 --> 01:38:51,863
(Worried about the ones working in the heat, )

2565
01:38:51,864 --> 01:38:54,164
(she goes out the gates.)

2566
01:38:55,264 --> 01:38:57,134
Gosh. They're done already.

2567
01:38:57,704 --> 01:38:59,834
- They're done already.
- What?

2568
01:39:00,404 --> 01:39:01,433
(What is she talking about?)

2569
01:39:01,434 --> 01:39:03,104
They're done. Gosh.

2570
01:39:03,504 --> 01:39:04,673
(Sang Hun peeks out through the gate.)

2571
01:39:04,674 --> 01:39:05,843
(What?)

2572
01:39:05,844 --> 01:39:07,844
- There's a sea now.
- How could this be possible?

2573
01:39:09,984 --> 01:39:12,483
- Gosh.
- She was an art major indeed.

2574
01:39:12,484 --> 01:39:14,713
Gosh. I'm shocked by her talents.

2575
01:39:14,714 --> 01:39:16,260
(The two are going crazy about the distant mural.)

2576
01:39:16,284 --> 01:39:17,444
Do you want to go and see it?

2577
01:39:17,924 --> 01:39:18,993
(Since the cooking is almost over, )

2578
01:39:18,994 --> 01:39:21,353
- They are good with their hands.
- I know.

2579
01:39:21,354 --> 01:39:22,754
(let's go see the mural ourselves.)

2580
01:39:24,394 --> 01:39:26,263
When did they match the colours?

2581
01:39:26,264 --> 01:39:27,694
- I know.
- It's hard to do so.

2582
01:39:28,494 --> 01:39:29,833
Gosh. They'll finish it today.

2583
01:39:29,834 --> 01:39:33,304
Goodness. After finishing that, they'll add fish tomorrow.

2584
01:39:33,874 --> 01:39:34,934
Come on.

2585
01:39:36,404 --> 01:39:39,914
(The three are so into the mural they didn't hear them coming.)

2586
01:39:40,614 --> 01:39:43,113
You're truly amazing.

2587
01:39:43,114 --> 01:39:44,184
Are you done cooking?

2588
01:39:44,714 --> 01:39:46,554
- Cooking isn't a big deal.
- From a distance,

2589
01:39:47,054 --> 01:39:49,153
it looks incredible. Do you just need to paint fish?

2590
01:39:49,154 --> 01:39:51,024
The sketch is amazing.

2591
01:39:51,384 --> 01:39:53,954
- It's incredible.
- Really?

2592
01:39:54,054 --> 01:39:55,323
- I'm in shock.
- Really?

2593
01:39:55,324 --> 01:39:56,794
- Really?
- Yes.

2594
01:39:57,864 --> 01:40:00,794
(Yoon Seo looks at the mural while they compliment it.)

2595
01:40:00,934 --> 01:40:01,934
- Really?
- Really?

2596
01:40:02,034 --> 01:40:04,633
Yes. Look how fast you did it.

2597
01:40:04,634 --> 01:40:06,204
Is it even possible?

2598
01:40:07,004 --> 01:40:09,244
Really? Does it look pretty from a distance?

2599
01:40:09,644 --> 01:40:12,314
- It looks magnificent.
- Gosh. It's really shocking.

2600
01:40:13,314 --> 01:40:14,613
I can't wait to see it from a distance too.

2601
01:40:14,614 --> 01:40:16,820
(It's high praise coming from Jung Ah, who's a hardcore thinker.)

2602
01:40:16,844 --> 01:40:19,384
Gosh. It'll look beautiful when they paint in the fish.

2603
01:40:20,614 --> 01:40:22,854
Gosh. The colours are great too.

2604
01:40:24,154 --> 01:40:26,654
We'll paint the fish and boats tomorrow, right?

2605
01:40:27,094 --> 01:40:28,354
You're so good at this.

2606
01:40:29,224 --> 01:40:31,763
- Are you done cooking already?
- Yes.

2607
01:40:31,764 --> 01:40:33,333
- It's simmering. We're all done.
- Really?

2608
01:40:33,334 --> 01:40:34,534
We just need to set the table.

2609
01:40:35,564 --> 01:40:38,704
Gosh. Yoon Seo is so cute. You're like a baby painter.

2610
01:40:39,474 --> 01:40:41,573
She is different because she learned the skills.

2611
01:40:41,574 --> 01:40:42,644
- Yes, of course.
- Right?

2612
01:40:42,904 --> 01:40:45,503
Gosh. Look how detailed You Seok is.

2613
01:40:45,504 --> 01:40:47,073
He's adding the whites and all.

2614
01:40:47,074 --> 01:40:49,514
Is it okay for You Seok to add white detail on his own?

2615
01:40:51,984 --> 01:40:53,553
I'm adding my artistic touch...

2616
01:40:53,554 --> 01:40:54,983
- to it.
- You're not an art major.

2617
01:40:54,984 --> 01:40:57,683
- I got the chief's permission.
- Really?

2618
01:40:57,684 --> 01:40:59,323
- Of course.
- Am I the chief?

2619
01:40:59,324 --> 01:41:01,444
(I've already discussed it with the art-major chief.)

2620
01:41:01,794 --> 01:41:04,524
I think he's mimicking the bubbles of the waves.

2621
01:41:05,264 --> 01:41:07,464
If you say it's mountains, it looks like mountains too.

2622
01:41:09,004 --> 01:41:10,484
Does it look like mountains? Hold on.

2623
01:41:11,404 --> 01:41:14,074
- I see. It's because of the green.
- I mean...

2624
01:41:15,104 --> 01:41:17,403
- They do look like mountains.
- If you think they are mountains...

2625
01:41:17,404 --> 01:41:19,844
Isn't it okay to call them mountains?

2626
01:41:20,214 --> 01:41:22,643
- You're right.
- The bottom layer is the sea.

2627
01:41:22,644 --> 01:41:24,860
The middle one can be the mountains while the top is the sky.

2628
01:41:24,884 --> 01:41:25,914
- Yes.
- It can be.

2629
01:41:26,854 --> 01:41:28,213
It's up to our interpretation, isn't it?

2630
01:41:28,214 --> 01:41:29,624
("Art is open to interpretation.")

2631
01:41:30,454 --> 01:41:33,053
When we add the fish and the boats tomorrow,

2632
01:41:33,054 --> 01:41:34,754
- it'll look like the sea.
- Totally.

2633
01:41:35,224 --> 01:41:37,494
(Sang Hun finds Yoon Seo adorable.)

2634
01:41:37,724 --> 01:41:39,193
- Let's hurry back.
- Yes, shall we?

2635
01:41:39,194 --> 01:41:40,263
(They leave as they have cooking to do.)

2636
01:41:40,264 --> 01:41:42,024
- It shouldn't be reduced too much.
- Right.

2637
01:41:42,464 --> 01:41:44,563
- Come back when you're done.
- Okay.

2638
01:41:44,564 --> 01:41:45,564
We're done.

2639
01:41:45,934 --> 01:41:47,203
Gosh. They've successfully painted...

2640
01:41:47,204 --> 01:41:49,943
so much in such a limited time.

2641
01:41:49,944 --> 01:41:51,003
(They're once again impressed by the younger ones' efforts.)

2642
01:41:51,004 --> 01:41:53,324
- It's truly amazing.
- Their backs are soaked with sweat.

2643
01:41:53,574 --> 01:41:55,574
They'll do fine. They'll finish it nicely.

2644
01:41:57,644 --> 01:41:59,724
Gosh. It feels much better now that the sun has set.

2645
01:42:00,254 --> 01:42:01,283
What colour is that?

2646
01:42:01,284 --> 01:42:02,284
(She goes straight to him with a roller...)

2647
01:42:02,284 --> 01:42:03,284
Use this one.

2648
01:42:03,285 --> 01:42:05,794
(and dips it without hesitation.)

2649
01:42:06,094 --> 01:42:09,064
Add the detail once I paint the background.

2650
01:42:09,494 --> 01:42:10,574
- Okay.
- Right under here.

2651
01:42:11,924 --> 01:42:12,993
I just need to paint the borders.

2652
01:42:12,994 --> 01:42:15,033
(Now, the three siblings are in perfect sync...)

2653
01:42:15,034 --> 01:42:17,064
(even without speaking a word.)

2654
01:42:17,234 --> 01:42:18,803
That's it. Good job, You Seok.

2655
01:42:18,804 --> 01:42:21,103
(In the wreckage)

2656
01:42:21,104 --> 01:42:23,373
(Left by the storm)

2657
01:42:23,374 --> 01:42:27,474
(Gentle waves roll on as if nothing ever happened)

2658
01:42:27,914 --> 01:42:32,184
(Flying creatures and swimming creatures)

2659
01:42:32,684 --> 01:42:34,983
(You've become paints)

2660
01:42:34,984 --> 01:42:38,154
(And now I'm a brush)

2661
01:42:39,994 --> 01:42:41,024
It's done.

2662
01:42:42,464 --> 01:42:44,493
(They've spent two hours at the same spot...)

2663
01:42:44,494 --> 01:42:46,494
(while painting again and again.)

2664
01:42:47,164 --> 01:42:49,563
(The empty gray wall has become a blue sea.)

2665
01:42:49,564 --> 01:42:52,203
- I'm so proud.
- Isn't it fun?

2666
01:42:52,204 --> 01:42:53,480
(The empty gray wall has become a blue sea.)

2667
01:42:53,504 --> 01:42:55,774
Painting is supposed to be very hard...

2668
01:42:56,344 --> 01:42:57,984
because you have to use your arm nonstop.

2669
01:42:58,304 --> 01:42:59,474
I'm so proud of myself.

2670
01:43:00,814 --> 01:43:02,014
I'm glad you are.

2671
01:43:02,374 --> 01:43:04,414
I know nothing about art.

2672
01:43:04,884 --> 01:43:05,953
Look at it from a distance, You Seok.

2673
01:43:05,954 --> 01:43:07,013
(Proud You Seok, and Sun Young and Yoon Seo can't leave the spot.)

2674
01:43:07,014 --> 01:43:08,460
- It looks pretty, though.
- I don't like it.

2675
01:43:08,484 --> 01:43:09,484
It's pretty.

2676
01:43:09,954 --> 01:43:11,624
I wanted to do better.

2677
01:43:11,884 --> 01:43:13,954
There's no problem. Let's do it tomorrow.

2678
01:43:15,024 --> 01:43:19,134
(What will be added to this painting tomorrow?)

2679
01:43:20,494 --> 01:43:21,533
Good job.

2680
01:43:21,534 --> 01:43:22,763
(Sun Young comes back with her head hung low.)

2681
01:43:22,764 --> 01:43:23,764
Good job.

2682
01:43:23,964 --> 01:43:25,033
(Good job!)

2683
01:43:25,034 --> 01:43:26,273
Well done, painters.

2684
01:43:26,274 --> 01:43:29,034
Yoon Seo and I are not satisfied with it.

2685
01:43:29,144 --> 01:43:30,204
From a distance?

2686
01:43:30,644 --> 01:43:33,414
I'm so proud of it, but they aren't happy with it.

2687
01:43:34,014 --> 01:43:35,074
I'm a perfectionist.

2688
01:43:36,114 --> 01:43:37,183
(Laughing)

2689
01:43:37,184 --> 01:43:38,344
Only You Seok is proud of it.

2690
01:43:39,184 --> 01:43:42,214
I'm so proud of it. I'm happy.

2691
01:43:42,954 --> 01:43:44,384
Right? Look at it from here.

2692
01:43:44,684 --> 01:43:46,923
- We can see it from here.
- It looks amazing from here.

2693
01:43:46,924 --> 01:43:48,154
It's so pretty.

2694
01:43:49,624 --> 01:43:51,164
It's great when we see it from here.

2695
01:43:51,764 --> 01:43:53,864
It'll look different tomorrow when it's dried.

2696
01:43:54,834 --> 01:43:57,064
- Gosh. I'm exhausted.
- Well done. Really.

2697
01:43:58,264 --> 01:43:59,633
(For those who are exhausted...)

2698
01:43:59,634 --> 01:44:00,873
Should we set the table now?

2699
01:44:00,874 --> 01:44:02,204
(For those who are exhausted...)

2700
01:44:02,474 --> 01:44:03,773
We should get ready to set the table.

2701
01:44:03,774 --> 01:44:05,814
(Today's highly anticipated dish is finally ready.)

2702
01:44:06,644 --> 01:44:09,413
It's crazy. I can't wait to have it.

2703
01:44:09,414 --> 01:44:11,134
(It looks so good they have to try it now.)

2704
01:44:11,314 --> 01:44:12,314
(She quickly takes out the ripened kimchi first.)

2705
01:44:12,314 --> 01:44:13,314
Are we eating now?

2706
01:44:13,315 --> 01:44:15,275
(She quickly takes out the ripened kimchi first.)

2707
01:44:17,384 --> 01:44:18,983
- I'll get the scissors.
- Gosh. It looks good.

2708
01:44:18,984 --> 01:44:21,623
- The kimchi smells incredible.
- Gosh.

2709
01:44:21,624 --> 01:44:23,544
(Well-simmered ripened kimchi that smells crazy)

2710
01:44:23,724 --> 01:44:24,794
Gosh. It looks good.

2711
01:44:26,064 --> 01:44:27,904
- Be careful. It's hot, isn't it?
- It's okay.

2712
01:44:29,934 --> 01:44:32,674
(The two are blown away by the chicken stew.)

2713
01:44:32,934 --> 01:44:34,904
- Won't this be enough for us?
- Yes.

2714
01:44:35,174 --> 01:44:36,174
It's too much.

2715
01:44:38,204 --> 01:44:39,273
It smells really good.

2716
01:44:39,274 --> 01:44:40,843
(They'll only have this much...)

2717
01:44:40,844 --> 01:44:42,604
(of the well-seasoned chicken and potatoes.)

2718
01:44:42,884 --> 01:44:45,183
(Carefully carrying it as it's heavy)

2719
01:44:45,184 --> 01:44:46,584
Gosh. It's crazy.

2720
01:44:48,054 --> 01:44:49,724
Gosh. It looks really amazing.

2721
01:44:51,024 --> 01:44:52,084
It looks so good.

2722
01:44:52,994 --> 01:44:54,754
Gosh. It smells incredible.

2723
01:44:54,854 --> 01:44:55,854
(Surprised)

2724
01:44:55,855 --> 01:44:57,124
(Dropping)

2725
01:44:57,394 --> 01:44:58,893
(Charging...)

2726
01:44:58,894 --> 01:45:01,634
(toward the ripened kimchi chicken stew)

2727
01:45:01,734 --> 01:45:02,734
Jung Ah.

2728
01:45:02,764 --> 01:45:03,764
Goodness.

2729
01:45:04,104 --> 01:45:07,034
Gosh. My goodness.

2730
01:45:07,234 --> 01:45:08,473
It's dried radish leaf soup.

2731
01:45:08,474 --> 01:45:09,774
- What?
- Sang Hun made it.

2732
01:45:11,304 --> 01:45:13,273
(Here's also the cooking genius's...)

2733
01:45:13,274 --> 01:45:14,974
(beef brisket and dried radish leaf soup!)

2734
01:45:15,344 --> 01:45:16,813
- Gosh.
- It looks so delicious.

2735
01:45:16,814 --> 01:45:17,943
(Sun Young and Yoon Seo regain their energy...)

2736
01:45:17,944 --> 01:45:19,184
(as the table is getting full.)

2737
01:45:19,954 --> 01:45:20,954
It's like a snack we have in the middle of work.

2738
01:45:20,955 --> 01:45:22,253
(They forget about the mural before they knew it.)

2739
01:45:22,254 --> 01:45:24,124
My goodness.

2740
01:45:24,324 --> 01:45:25,654
My goodness.

2741
01:45:27,094 --> 01:45:29,393
(The siblings' first dinner in Yeosu for the younger siblings...)

2742
01:45:29,394 --> 01:45:31,724
(who worked so hard)

2743
01:45:33,194 --> 01:45:34,893
(Jung Ah's ripened kimchi chicken stew...)

2744
01:45:34,894 --> 01:45:36,564
(with tangy umami)

2745
01:45:37,734 --> 01:45:39,703
(Sang Hun's beef brisket and dried radish leaf soup...)

2746
01:45:39,704 --> 01:45:41,674
(with rich and aromatic flavours)

2747
01:45:42,404 --> 01:45:45,904
(They sit in the shade of the protected tree...)

2748
01:45:47,244 --> 01:45:51,044
(with the small port as a background.)

2749
01:45:52,014 --> 01:45:53,753
(They can't help but clap.)

2750
01:45:53,754 --> 01:45:55,754
Goodness. Our cooking genius.

2751
01:45:56,124 --> 01:45:58,184
I can't wait to try the soup Sang Hun made.

2752
01:45:58,684 --> 01:46:00,023
- It's dried radish leaf soup. Yes.
- Are these dried radish leaves?

2753
01:46:00,024 --> 01:46:02,724
- It's dried radish leaf soup.
- It looks like meat soup.

2754
01:46:03,364 --> 01:46:05,393
- It looks like meat soup.
- It's made with meat.

2755
01:46:05,394 --> 01:46:07,164
(How does it taste?)

2756
01:46:07,234 --> 01:46:09,064
(Humming)

2757
01:46:09,804 --> 01:46:10,804
It tastes good.

2758
01:46:13,504 --> 01:46:17,004
(Eating a lot of radish leaves)

2759
01:46:17,874 --> 01:46:19,743
(How is it?)

2760
01:46:19,744 --> 01:46:21,514
- It tastes just like meat soup.
- Yes.

2761
01:46:22,014 --> 01:46:24,943
- I never had it before.
- Dried radish leaves are good.

2762
01:46:24,944 --> 01:46:25,944
Right.

2763
01:46:25,945 --> 01:46:28,505
(Dried radish leaves seasoned with beef brisket's savoury flavour)

2764
01:46:29,324 --> 01:46:30,384
Dried radish leaf soup?

2765
01:46:34,354 --> 01:46:35,823
(Gasping)

2766
01:46:35,824 --> 01:46:37,564
(Enlightened)

2767
01:46:38,464 --> 01:46:39,993
It's very deep and rich.

2768
01:46:39,994 --> 01:46:41,874
- I mean the broth.
- It's just like meat soup.

2769
01:46:42,964 --> 01:46:46,933
(The professional home cook tries a lot of chunks.)

2770
01:46:46,934 --> 01:46:48,473
Sang Hun, you're an amazing cook.

2771
01:46:48,474 --> 01:46:49,474
- Seriously.
- Dried radish leaves...

2772
01:46:49,475 --> 01:46:50,673
Your soup is delicious.

2773
01:46:50,674 --> 01:46:51,914
How is it spicy and refreshing?

2774
01:46:53,214 --> 01:46:54,214
What's in it?

2775
01:46:55,414 --> 01:46:58,444
He made the broth properly with anchovies.

2776
01:46:59,084 --> 01:47:00,114
- Right?
- Yes.

2777
01:47:00,284 --> 01:47:02,444
- Is that why the flavour is deep?
